+# Document Lifecycle
+
+Document ID: GOV-0002
+Version: 0.1.0
+Status: Draft
+Owner:
+Created:
+Last Updated:
+Authority: Governance
+Supersedes:
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+Define the lifecycle of repository documents from creation through archival.
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle
+
+## Draft
+
+The document is under active development.
+
+Content may change substantially.
+
+---
+
+## Active
+
+The document is considered authoritative.
+
+Changes should be deliberate and documented.
+
+---
+
+## Superseded
+
+The document has been replaced by a newer version.
+
+It is retained for historical reference.
+
+---
+
+## Archived
+
+The document is no longer maintained but remains part of the repository history.
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle Rules
+
+- Every document begins as Draft.
+- Active documents represent the current authoritative version.
+- Superseded documents should reference their replacement.
+- Archived documents should not be modified except for preservation purposes.
+
+---
+
+# Stewardship
+
+Documents evolve.
+
+Knowledge should not be deleted simply because it has changed.
+
+Historical reasoning is valuable.
+
+---
+
+# References
+
+- GOV-0001 Repository Principles
+- DOCUMENT_METADATA.md
