+# Difference Engine Governance
+
+## Purpose
+
+The Governance repository establishes the constitutional authority, institutional responsibilities, and governance procedures of the Difference Engine.
+
+Governance defines **what the institution is authorized to do**. Architecture defines **how systems are designed**. Implementations define **how systems are built**.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Purpose
+
+This repository exists to:
+
+- Define constitutional authority.
+- Establish institutional governance.
+- Preserve institutional continuity.
+- Maintain governance history.
+- Provide traceability between governance and implementation.
+
+---
+
+# Governance Principles
+
+The Difference Engine is governed by durable artifacts rather than conversational state.
+
+Core principles include:
+
+- Authority is constitutional.
+- Governance precedes implementation.
+- Implementations derive from governance.
+- Artifacts preserve institutional knowledge.
+- Records preserve institutional history.
+- Provenance shall never be lost.
+
+---
+
+# Document Families
+
+## Constitutions
+
+| Prefix | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| DE-CON | Difference Engine Constitution |
+| DE-CORE | Core Constitutional Principles |
+
+## Branch Constitutions
+
+| Prefix | Branch |
+|---------|--------|
+| DE-ENG | Engineering |
+| DE-OPS | Operations |
+| DE-INT | Integration |
+| DE-ORG | Origins |
+| DE-RES | Research |
+
+## Governance Specifications
+
+| Prefix | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| DE-GOV | Governance Specifications |
+
+## Institutional Context Documents
+
+| Prefix | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| ICD | Institutional Context Documents |
+
+## Ratification Records
+
+| Prefix | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| RR | Ratification Records |
+
+---
+
+# Reading Order
+
+1. DE-CON-001
+2. DE-CORE-001
+3. Branch Constitutions
+4. Governance Specifications
+5. Institutional Context Documents
+6. Ratification Records
+
+---
+
+# Relationship to the Repository
+
+Governance is one domain within the Difference Engine repository.
+
+The repository is organized into:
+
+- Governance
+- Architecture
+- Stewardship
+- Evidence
+- Knowledge
+- Implementations
+- Publications
+- Archive
+- Review
+- Laboratory
+- Utilities
+
+---
+
+# Relationship to Engineering
+
+Engineering implementations shall:
+
+- derive from constitutional authority;
+- comply with governance specifications;
+- preserve provenance; and
+- maintain traceability to governing artifacts.
+
+Engineering shall not expand constitutional authority.
+
+---
+
+# Publication Philosophy
+
+Conversations are transient.
+
+Artifacts are durable.
+
+The purpose of Governance is to preserve institutional knowledge as structured, versioned, and traceable artifacts.
+
+---
+
+**Repository:** ADE
+
+**Directory:** `10_Governance`
+
+**Publication Package:** CSP-001
