@@ -0,0 +1,209 @@
+# Contents
+````markdown
+# Artifact Lifecycle Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Artifact Lifecycle Specification defines the canonical lifecycle of every repository artifact from initial ingestion through archival.
+
+Every artifact SHALL occupy exactly one lifecycle state at any given time.
+
+Lifecycle transitions SHALL be explicit and recorded.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Every artifact has a lifecycle.
+- Lifecycle changes are recorded.
+- State transitions preserve provenance.
+- History is append-only.
+- Artifacts are never silently removed.
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle States
+
+## Imported
+
+The artifact has entered the ingestion system.
+
+No structural parsing has occurred.
+
+---
+
+## Parsed
+
+Structural parsing has completed successfully.
+
+Structural observations have been recorded.
+
+---
+
+## Validated
+
+Validation has completed.
+
+Results have been recorded.
+
+---
+
+## Queued
+
+Queue candidates have been generated.
+
+The artifact awaits downstream processing.
+
+---
+
+## Mapped
+
+Repository Mapping has completed.
+
+Repository relationships have been identified.
+
+---
+
+## Under Review
+
+Human or governance review is underway.
+
+Review decisions are pending.
+
+---
+
+## Promoted
+
+The artifact has been approved for canonical promotion.
+
+Promotion history has been recorded.
+
+---
+
+## Published
+
+The canonical artifact has been published to its repository destination.
+
+Repository indexes have been updated.
+
+---
+
+## Superseded
+
+A newer canonical artifact has replaced this artifact.
+
+The artifact remains preserved.
+
+---
+
+## Archived
+
+The artifact is retained for historical purposes.
+
+Archived artifacts remain searchable.
+
+---
+
+# State Transitions
+
+Permitted transitions include:
+
+Imported
+
+↓
+
+Parsed
+
+↓
+
+Validated
+
+↓
+
+Queued
+
+↓
+
+Mapped
+
+↓
+
+Under Review
+
+↓
+
+Promoted
+
+↓
+
+Published
+
+Published artifacts MAY transition to:
+
+- Superseded
+- Archived
+
+Rollback transitions SHALL be explicitly recorded.
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle Events
+
+Every transition SHALL record:
+
+- Event ID
+- Previous State
+- New State
+- Timestamp
+- Responsible Service
+- Responsible Version
+- Reviewer (if applicable)
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+A lifecycle transition SHALL NOT occur unless:
+
+- Required predecessor state exists.
+- Required records exist.
+- Provenance is complete.
+
+---
+
+# Failure Handling
+
+Failed transitions SHALL:
+
+- Preserve current state.
+- Record failure.
+- Preserve partial processing.
+- Never discard artifacts.
+
+---
+
+# Relationship to Provenance
+
+Lifecycle history becomes part of the artifact provenance.
+
+Lifecycle events SHALL be immutable.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Artifacts evolve.
+
+Evidence does not.
+
+The lifecycle records the evolution of repository stewardship rather than changes to the underlying evidence.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
