+# Artifact Schema
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Artifact Schema defines the canonical structural representation for all repository artifacts.
+
+Every ingested object SHALL conform to this schema prior to semantic processing.
+
+Specialized schemas extend this specification.
+
+---
+
+# Artifact Hierarchy
+
+Artifact
+
+├── Metadata
+
+├── Provenance
+
+├── Content
+
+├── Structure
+
+├── Assets
+
+├── References
+
+├── Queue Candidates
+
+├── Validation
+
+└── Lifecycle
+
+---
+
+# Metadata
+
+Required:
+
+- Artifact ID
+- Title
+- Artifact Type
+- Source Platform
+- Original Filename
+- Import Timestamp
+- Repository Path
+- Version
+- Language
+
+Optional:
+
+- Tags
+- Author
+- Description
+
+---
+
+# Provenance
+
+Required:
+
+- Source Artifact
+- Original Location
+- Parser Version
+- Import Method
+- Checksum (future)
+- Import Timestamp
+
+Every artifact SHALL preserve provenance.
+
+---
+
+# Content
+
+The original content SHALL remain unmodified.
+
+Normalized representations MAY exist but SHALL NOT replace the source.
+
+Examples:
+
+- Original PDF
+- Extracted text
+- Markdown conversion
+- OCR transcript
+
+---
+
+# Structure
+
+Structural observations only.
+
+Examples include:
+
+- Sections
+- Paragraphs
+- Tables
+- Lists
+- Code Blocks
+- Headings
+- Conversation Turns
+- Attachments
+
+No semantic interpretation occurs here.
+
+---
+
+# Assets
+
+Reusable components extracted from the artifact.
+
+Examples:
+
+- Markdown templates
+- JSON
+- YAML
+- Code
+- Diagrams
+- Charts
+- Graphs
+- Tables
+- Checklists
+- Folder structures
+- Specifications
+- Prompts
+
+Assets SHALL retain provenance.
+
+---
+
+# References
+
+Capture references to:
+
+- Repository artifacts
+- External URLs
+- Files
+- Images
+- Publications
+- Standards
+- Code repositories
+
+References remain unresolved until Repository Mapping.
+
+---
+
+# Queue Candidates
+
+Artifacts MAY produce candidates for one or more processing queues.
+
+Queue assignment is provisional.
+
+Promotion requires review.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Every artifact SHALL validate:
+
+✓ Metadata complete
+
+✓ Provenance complete
+
+✓ Original preserved
+
+✓ Structural observations complete
+
+✓ Assets extracted
+
+✓ References captured
+
+✓ Queue candidates generated
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle
+
+Every artifact exists in one lifecycle state.
+
+States:
+
+- Imported
+- Parsed
+- Queued
+- Reviewed
+- Mapped
+- Promoted
+- Archived
+
+Lifecycle state SHALL be explicit.
+
+---
+
+# Extension Model
+
+Specialized schemas extend this specification.
+
+Examples:
+
+- Conversation Schema
+- PDF Schema
+- Image Schema
+- Research Paper Schema
+- Governance Document Schema
+- Observation Schema
+
+Extensions inherit this schema.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+Artifacts are immutable evidence.
+
+Derived products are separate artifacts.
+
+No transformation replaces the source.
+
+Every derivative retains lineage.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
