+# Asset Schema
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Asset Schema defines the canonical representation of reusable assets extracted from repository artifacts.
+
+Assets are repository objects derived from artifacts.
+
+Assets are not independent evidence.
+
+They retain lineage to their parent artifact.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Assets are extracted, not authored.
+- Assets retain complete provenance.
+- Assets are reusable.
+- Assets are immutable.
+- Assets never replace their parent artifact.
+
+---
+
+# Required Fields
+
+Every asset SHALL contain:
+
+- Asset ID
+- Parent Artifact ID
+- Asset Type
+- Title
+- Content
+- Provenance Record
+- Extraction Timestamp
+- Parser Version
+
+---
+
+# Optional Fields
+
+Assets MAY include:
+
+- Language
+- Format
+- Tags
+- Description
+- Related Asset IDs
+- Related Artifact IDs
+- Reviewer Notes
+
+---
+
+# Supported Asset Types
+
+Examples include:
+
+- Markdown
+- Template
+- Prompt
+- Specification
+- JSON
+- YAML
+- XML
+- Python
+- Bash
+- PowerShell
+- SQL
+- Mermaid Diagram
+- ASCII Diagram
+- Table
+- Chart
+- Graph
+- Checklist
+- Decision Tree
+- Folder Structure
+- Configuration
+- Citation
+- Regular Expression
+
+Additional asset types MAY be defined through future specifications.
+
+---
+
+# Asset Content
+
+Asset content SHALL preserve the extracted structure.
+
+Formatting SHALL be retained whenever practical.
+
+Normalization SHALL NOT destroy information.
+
+---
+
+# Provenance
+
+Every asset SHALL retain:
+
+- Parent Artifact ID
+- Source Location
+- Extraction Method
+- Parser Version
+- Timestamp
+
+Assets SHALL never lose their lineage.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+A valid asset SHALL:
+
+- Reference an existing parent artifact.
+- Declare an asset type.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Preserve extracted content.
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle
+
+Assets SHALL exist in one of the following states:
+
+- Extracted
+- Validated
+- Indexed
+- Referenced
+- Archived
+
+Assets SHALL NOT be deleted solely because the parent artifact changes.
+
+---
+
+# Relationship to Artifacts
+
+Artifacts contain evidence.
+
+Assets expose reusable components of that evidence.
+
+Multiple assets MAY originate from a single artifact.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Artifacts preserve history.
+
+Assets preserve utility.
+
+Together they create a reusable institutional memory.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
