+# Conversation Schema
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Conversation Schema defines the canonical structural representation of conversational artifacts.
+
+It separates structural observation from semantic interpretation.
+
+Conversation parsers SHALL target this schema regardless of source platform.
+
+---
+
+# Schema Overview
+
+Conversation Artifact
+
+├── Metadata
+
+├── Provenance
+
+├── Participants
+
+├── Structure
+
+├── References
+
+├── Structural Assets
+
+├── Queue Candidates
+
+└── Validation
+
+---
+
+# Metadata
+
+Required fields:
+
+- Artifact ID
+- Title
+- Source Platform
+- Import Date
+- Original Filename
+- Version
+- Language
+
+---
+
+# Provenance
+
+Required fields:
+
+- Source Artifact
+- Original Location
+- Parser Version
+- Import Timestamp
+- Repository Path
+
+---
+
+# Participants
+
+Each participant shall include:
+
+- Identifier
+- Role
+- Display Name (if available)
+
+No assumptions shall be made regarding identity.
+
+---
+
+# Structure
+
+The parser SHALL preserve chronological order.
+
+Each conversational turn shall include:
+
+- Turn ID
+- Speaker
+- Timestamp (if available)
+- Raw Content
+- Attachments
+- References
+
+No summarization occurs here.
+
+---
+
+# References
+
+Capture references to:
+
+- Files
+- URLs
+- Repository Artifacts
+- External Documents
+- Images
+- Code
+- Specifications
+
+References remain unresolved until Repository Mapping.
+
+---
+
+# Structural Assets
+
+Capture reusable assets without interpretation.
+
+Examples include:
+
+## Markdown
+
+- Templates
+- Checklists
+- Specifications
+
+---
+
+## Code
+
+- Python
+- JSON
+- YAML
+- Bash
+- PowerShell
+- Configuration
+
+---
+
+## Visualizations
+
+- Mermaid
+- ASCII diagrams
+- Flowcharts
+- Graphs
+- Charts
+- Tables
+
+---
+
+## Prompts
+
+Reusable prompt structures.
+
+---
+
+## File Structures
+
+Repository layouts.
+
+Folder trees.
+
+Naming conventions.
+
+---
+
+# Queue Candidates
+
+Structural parsing SHALL populate candidate queues without interpretation.
+
+Possible queues include:
+
+- Decision Review
+- Concept
+- Observation
+- Tool
+- Template
+- Visualization
+- Infrastructure
+- Cross-Reference
+- Open Question
+- Constitutional
+- Promotion
+- Meta-Improvement
+
+Queue assignment is structural only.
+
+Promotion requires later review.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Every parsed conversation shall validate:
+
+✓ Chronology preserved
+
+✓ Raw text preserved
+
+✓ Provenance complete
+
+✓ References captured
+
+✓ Structural assets extracted
+
+✓ Queue candidates generated
+
+---
+
+# Parser Responsibilities
+
+The parser SHALL:
+
+- Preserve evidence
+- Preserve chronology
+- Preserve provenance
+- Preserve reusable artifacts
+
+The parser SHALL NOT:
+
+- Rewrite content
+- Summarize discussions
+- Merge concepts
+- Promote knowledge
+- Interpret intent
+- Modify evidence
+
+Those responsibilities belong to downstream services.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+A conversation is evidence.
+
+The parser preserves evidence.
+
+Subsequent services derive knowledge.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
