+# Event Catalog Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Event Catalog Specification defines the canonical catalog of event types recognized by the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+The Event Model defines the structure of events.
+
+The Event Catalog defines the vocabulary of events.
+
+Together they establish a consistent event language across the repository.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Event names are stable.
+- Event meanings are explicit.
+- Event types are versioned.
+- Event semantics remain consistent.
+- Events describe completed observations.
+
+---
+
+# Event Naming Standard
+
+Event names SHOULD follow the pattern:
+
+Subject + Action
+
+Examples:
+
+- Artifact Imported
+- Parsing Completed
+- Validation Failed
+- Queue Candidate Created
+- Publication Completed
+
+Names SHALL describe observable facts.
+
+---
+
+# Intake Events
+
+These events describe artifact acquisition.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Artifact Imported | Source artifact successfully accepted |
+| Artifact Rejected | Artifact rejected before ingestion |
+| Metadata Generated | Initial metadata created |
+| Provenance Initialized | Provenance record established |
+
+---
+
+# Parser Events
+
+These events describe parser execution.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Parsing Started | Parser execution began |
+| Parsing Completed | Parser completed successfully |
+| Parsing Failed | Parser terminated unsuccessfully |
+| Parsing Partially Completed | Partial results preserved |
+
+---
+
+# Asset Events
+
+These events describe asset extraction.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Asset Extraction Started | Asset extraction initiated |
+| Asset Extracted | Asset successfully extracted |
+| Asset Validation Failed | Extracted asset failed validation |
+| Asset Archived | Asset archived |
+
+---
+
+# Reference Events
+
+These events describe reference discovery.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Reference Discovered | Reference observed |
+| Reference Validated | Reference verified |
+| Reference Resolved | Reference linked |
+| Reference Archived | Reference archived |
+
+---
+
+# Queue Events
+
+These events describe queue management.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Queue Candidate Created | Candidate generated |
+| Queue Candidate Updated | Candidate modified |
+| Queue Candidate Approved | Candidate accepted |
+| Queue Candidate Rejected | Candidate rejected |
+| Queue Candidate Removed | Candidate removed |
+
+---
+
+# Validation Events
+
+These events describe validation activity.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Validation Started | Validation initiated |
+| Validation Passed | Validation succeeded |
+| Validation Failed | Validation failed |
+| Validation Warning Generated | Non-critical issue detected |
+
+---
+
+# Mapping Events
+
+These events describe repository mapping.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Mapping Started | Mapping initiated |
+| Relationship Discovered | Relationship identified |
+| Duplicate Detected | Duplicate candidate found |
+| Mapping Completed | Mapping finished |
+
+---
+
+# Governance Events
+
+These events describe governance workflows.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Review Started | Review initiated |
+| Review Completed | Review completed |
+| Promotion Approved | Promotion accepted |
+| Promotion Rejected | Promotion denied |
+| Publication Authorized | Publication approved |
+
+---
+
+# Publication Events
+
+These events describe repository publication.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Publication Started | Publication initiated |
+| Publication Completed | Publication completed |
+| Repository Index Updated | Repository indexes refreshed |
+
+---
+
+# Lifecycle Events
+
+These events describe artifact lifecycle transitions.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Lifecycle State Changed | Artifact entered a new lifecycle state |
+| Artifact Archived | Artifact archived |
+| Artifact Superseded | Artifact replaced |
+| Artifact Restored | Archived artifact restored |
+
+---
+
+# Operational Events
+
+These events describe operational activity.
+
+| Event | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| Service Started | Service initialized |
+| Service Stopped | Service terminated |
+| Configuration Loaded | Configuration applied |
+| Configuration Updated | Configuration changed |
+| Health Check Completed | Health verification executed |
+| Recovery Completed | Recovery procedure completed |
+
+---
+
+# Event Versioning
+
+Each event definition SHALL specify:
+
+- Event Version
+- Effective Date
+- Status
+- Related Specifications
+
+Changes to event semantics SHALL increment the event version.
+
+---
+
+# Event Deprecation
+
+Deprecated events SHALL:
+
+- Remain documented.
+- Record replacement events.
+- Preserve historical compatibility.
+- Never invalidate historical event records.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Every event recorded by the repository SHALL:
+
+- Match a catalog definition.
+- Conform to the Event Model Specification.
+- Validate required metadata.
+- Preserve chronological consistency.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+A repository speaks through its events.
+
+The Event Model defines the grammar.
+
+The Event Catalog defines the vocabulary.
+
+Together they create a precise and durable language for describing the life of the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
