+# Contents
+````markdown
+# Ingestion Pipeline Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Ingestion Pipeline Specification defines the canonical sequence of services that transform source artifacts into validated repository artifacts.
+
+The pipeline is deterministic.
+
+Each stage has a single responsibility.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- One responsibility per stage.
+- Stages communicate through well-defined artifacts.
+- Every stage preserves provenance.
+- Every stage is independently testable.
+- Stages may be replaced without altering the pipeline contract.
+
+---
+
+# Canonical Pipeline
+
+Artifact
+
+↓
+
+Artifact Intake
+
+↓
+
+Structural Parsing
+
+↓
+
+Asset Extraction
+
+↓
+
+Reference Extraction
+
+↓
+
+Queue Candidate Generation
+
+↓
+
+Validation
+
+↓
+
+Repository Mapping
+
+↓
+
+Review
+
+↓
+
+Canonical Promotion
+
+↓
+
+Publication
+
+↓
+
+Repository Index Update
+
+---
+
+# Stage 1 — Artifact Intake
+
+Purpose:
+
+Accept source artifacts.
+
+Outputs:
+
+- Artifact Record
+- Initial Metadata
+- Provenance Record
+
+---
+
+# Stage 2 — Structural Parsing
+
+Purpose:
+
+Capture observable structure.
+
+Outputs:
+
+- Structural Representation
+- Sections
+- Chronology
+- Assets
+- References
+
+No interpretation occurs.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 3 — Asset Extraction
+
+Purpose:
+
+Extract reusable repository assets.
+
+Examples:
+
+- Markdown
+- JSON
+- YAML
+- Code
+- Diagrams
+- Templates
+- Tables
+- Prompts
+
+Assets retain provenance.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 4 — Reference Extraction
+
+Purpose:
+
+Capture all internal and external references.
+
+References remain unresolved.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 5 — Queue Candidate Generation
+
+Purpose:
+
+Generate provisional queue candidates.
+
+No promotion decisions occur.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 6 — Validation
+
+Purpose:
+
+Verify specification compliance.
+
+Validation records findings.
+
+Validation does not modify artifacts.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 7 — Repository Mapping
+
+Purpose:
+
+Discover repository relationships.
+
+Mapping identifies:
+
+- Related artifacts
+- Duplicates
+- Extensions
+- Supersession candidates
+
+Mapping performs no modifications.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 8 — Review
+
+Purpose:
+
+Evaluate queue candidates and mapping results.
+
+Review governs repository decisions.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 9 — Canonical Promotion
+
+Purpose:
+
+Create canonical repository knowledge.
+
+Promotion preserves lineage.
+
+Promotion never destroys evidence.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 10 — Publication
+
+Purpose:
+
+Publish canonical artifacts.
+
+Publication updates repository structures.
+
+---
+
+# Stage 11 — Repository Index Update
+
+Purpose:
+
+Update repository indexes.
+
+Examples:
+
+- Artifact Index
+- Asset Index
+- Relationship Index
+- Search Index
+- Knowledge Graph
+
+Indexes SHALL remain consistent.
+
+---
+
+# Pipeline Guarantees
+
+The pipeline SHALL:
+
+- Preserve evidence.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Preserve chronology.
+- Produce deterministic outputs.
+- Record every stage.
+
+---
+
+# Pipeline Failures
+
+Failures SHALL:
+
+- Record the failure.
+- Preserve completed work.
+- Preserve source artifacts.
+- Permit restart from the appropriate stage.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+The pipeline is a chain of custody.
+
+Each stage contributes information.
+
+No stage assumes authority beyond its responsibility.
+
+Together they transform evidence into governed institutional knowledge.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
