+# Operational Readiness Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Operational Readiness Specification defines the minimum operational requirements that SHALL be satisfied before Repository Ingestion Framework components are considered suitable for production use.
+
+Implementation alone does not constitute operational readiness.
+
+Operational readiness demonstrates that a component can be deployed, monitored, maintained, and recovered.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Operations are part of engineering.
+- Reliability is measurable.
+- Failures are expected.
+- Recovery is planned.
+- Operational evidence is recorded.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+Operational readiness applies to:
+
+- Services
+- Parsers
+- Validation engines
+- Repository mapping
+- Queue generation
+- Governance workflows
+- Supporting infrastructure
+
+---
+
+# Readiness Categories
+
+Operational readiness SHALL evaluate:
+
+- Functional Readiness
+- Operational Readiness
+- Monitoring Readiness
+- Recovery Readiness
+- Security Readiness
+- Documentation Readiness
+
+---
+
+# Functional Readiness
+
+The component SHALL:
+
+- Meet its governing specification.
+- Pass required tests.
+- Produce deterministic outputs.
+- Validate successfully.
+
+---
+
+# Operational Readiness
+
+The component SHALL:
+
+- Start successfully.
+- Shut down gracefully.
+- Handle expected workloads.
+- Produce execution reports.
+- Record operational events.
+
+---
+
+# Monitoring Readiness
+
+Operational monitoring SHOULD include:
+
+- Execution counts
+- Success rates
+- Failure rates
+- Processing duration
+- Resource utilization
+- Queue depth (where applicable)
+
+Monitoring SHALL support troubleshooting.
+
+---
+
+# Recovery Readiness
+
+The component SHALL support:
+
+- Failure detection
+- Safe restart
+- Partial recovery
+- Retry mechanisms
+- Preservation of repository integrity
+
+Recovery SHALL NOT compromise provenance.
+
+---
+
+# Security Readiness
+
+Operational deployments SHOULD verify:
+
+- Configuration integrity
+- Access controls
+- Audit logging
+- Dependency verification
+- Sensitive data protection
+
+Security controls SHALL align with repository governance.
+
+---
+
+# Documentation Readiness
+
+Operational documentation SHOULD include:
+
+- Purpose
+- Dependencies
+- Configuration
+- Startup procedure
+- Shutdown procedure
+- Recovery procedure
+- Known limitations
+- Troubleshooting guidance
+
+Documentation SHALL remain synchronized with implementation.
+
+---
+
+# Deployment Criteria
+
+A component SHOULD NOT be deployed unless:
+
+- Specifications are approved.
+- Required tests pass.
+- Validation succeeds.
+- Documentation is complete.
+- Operational review is complete.
+
+Deployment decisions SHALL be documented.
+
+---
+
+# Operational Metrics
+
+Operational health MAY be evaluated using:
+
+- Availability
+- Mean processing time
+- Error rate
+- Recovery time
+- Validation success rate
+- Queue throughput
+- Repository consistency
+
+Metrics SHOULD be collected consistently.
+
+---
+
+# Operational Review
+
+Operational reviews SHOULD confirm:
+
+- Readiness requirements satisfied
+- Outstanding risks identified
+- Monitoring operational
+- Recovery procedures validated
+- Documentation current
+
+Review findings SHALL become repository records.
+
+---
+
+# Continuous Operations
+
+Operational readiness SHALL be maintained through:
+
+- Regular testing
+- Dependency updates
+- Documentation review
+- Monitoring verification
+- Periodic operational assessment
+
+Operational readiness is an ongoing responsibility.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Building a component demonstrates engineering capability.
+
+Operating that component reliably demonstrates institutional capability.
+
+The Repository Ingestion Framework is successful not merely when it functions, but when it can be trusted to continue functioning under sustained operational use.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
