+# Parser Development Guide
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Parser Development Guide provides implementation guidance for creating artifact parsers within the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Parsers are responsible for observing artifacts and producing structured representations.
+
+Parsers SHALL preserve evidence without interpretation.
+
+---
+
+# Parser Responsibilities
+
+Every parser SHALL:
+
+- Accept supported artifact types.
+- Produce deterministic output.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Record parsing diagnostics.
+- Never modify source artifacts.
+
+---
+
+# Parser Scope
+
+A parser is responsible for observing:
+
+- Document structure
+- Sections
+- Headings
+- Lists
+- Tables
+- Code blocks
+- Images
+- Links
+- Metadata
+- Embedded assets
+
+A parser SHALL NOT infer meaning.
+
+---
+
+# Parser Pipeline
+
+Each parser SHOULD perform the following sequence:
+
+1. Load artifact.
+2. Verify format.
+3. Parse structure.
+4. Extract observable elements.
+5. Record provenance.
+6. Generate parser report.
+7. Return structured representation.
+
+---
+
+# Supported Outputs
+
+Parsers MAY produce:
+
+- Structural representation
+- Asset candidates
+- Reference candidates
+- Metadata
+- Diagnostics
+
+Outputs SHALL conform to repository schemas.
+
+---
+
+# Error Handling
+
+Parsers SHALL distinguish between:
+
+- Invalid artifacts
+- Unsupported formats
+- Partial parsing
+- Recoverable errors
+- Fatal errors
+
+Whenever possible, partial results SHOULD be preserved.
+
+---
+
+# Determinism
+
+Given identical input and parser version:
+
+- Output SHALL be identical.
+- Identifiers SHALL remain stable where applicable.
+- Parsing order SHALL remain consistent.
+
+---
+
+# Performance
+
+Parsers SHOULD:
+
+- Stream large artifacts when practical.
+- Avoid unnecessary memory usage.
+- Minimize repeated processing.
+- Report execution statistics.
+
+Performance optimizations SHALL NOT compromise correctness.
+
+---
+
+# Parser Reports
+
+Each parser execution SHOULD produce a report containing:
+
+- Parser name
+- Parser version
+- Artifact ID
+- Timestamp
+- Processing duration
+- Warnings
+- Errors
+- Output summary
+
+Parser reports support debugging and auditing.
+
+---
+
+# Testing Requirements
+
+Every parser SHOULD include tests covering:
+
+- Valid inputs
+- Invalid inputs
+- Empty artifacts
+- Large artifacts
+- Edge cases
+- Regression scenarios
+
+Test artifacts SHOULD remain under version control.
+
+---
+
+# Extensibility
+
+New parsers SHOULD:
+
+- Reuse shared services.
+- Follow repository schemas.
+- Implement existing service contracts.
+- Avoid introducing parser-specific conventions without governance approval.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+A parser is an observer.
+
+Its purpose is to faithfully record what exists, not to decide what it means.
+
+Reliable observation is the foundation upon which repository knowledge is built.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
