+# Contents
+````markdown
+# Schema Governance Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Schema Governance Specification defines how repository schemas are created, modified, versioned, approved, and retired.
+
+Schemas are constitutional documents.
+
+They SHALL evolve deliberately.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Schemas are versioned.
+- Changes are explicit.
+- History is preserved.
+- Compatibility is preferred.
+- Governance precedes implementation.
+
+---
+
+# Schema Authority
+
+Repository schemas define the canonical structure of repository data.
+
+Implementations SHALL conform to schemas.
+
+Schemas SHALL NOT conform to implementations.
+
+---
+
+# Schema Lifecycle
+
+Every schema SHALL exist in one of the following states:
+
+- Draft
+- Review
+- Approved
+- Active
+- Superseded
+- Archived
+
+---
+
+# Versioning
+
+Schemas SHALL use semantic versioning.
+
+Examples:
+
+- v0.1
+- v0.5
+- v1.0
+- v1.1
+- v2.0
+
+---
+
+# Change Categories
+
+## Editorial
+
+Grammar.
+
+Formatting.
+
+Clarification.
+
+No structural changes.
+
+---
+
+## Minor
+
+New optional fields.
+
+Additional examples.
+
+Backward-compatible improvements.
+
+---
+
+## Major
+
+Breaking structural changes.
+
+Removed fields.
+
+Changed behavior.
+
+Changed required elements.
+
+---
+
+# Required Schema Metadata
+
+Every schema SHALL declare:
+
+- Name
+- Version
+- Status
+- Owner
+- Date Created
+- Date Modified
+- Parent Specification
+- Dependencies
+
+---
+
+# Approval
+
+Schema approval SHALL record:
+
+- Reviewer
+- Approval Date
+- Approved Version
+- Notes
+
+Approval records SHALL become part of repository governance.
+
+---
+
+# Deprecation
+
+Superseded schemas SHALL:
+
+- Remain accessible.
+- Retain provenance.
+- Record replacement schemas.
+- Preserve historical compatibility.
+
+Schemas SHALL NOT be silently removed.
+
+---
+
+# Implementation Compatibility
+
+Implementations SHALL declare:
+
+- Supported Schema Version
+- Unsupported Features
+- Compatibility Notes
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Every schema SHALL validate:
+
+- Internal consistency.
+- Required metadata.
+- Version correctness.
+- Cross-specification references.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Schemas define the language of the repository.
+
+Governance protects that language.
+
+Stable schemas create stable systems.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
