+# Service Development Guide
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Service Development Guide provides implementation guidance for developing repository services.
+
+Services perform the work of the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Each service is responsible for a single capability and communicates through well-defined contracts.
+
+---
+
+# Service Principles
+
+Every service SHALL:
+
+- Have a single responsibility.
+- Implement an approved service contract.
+- Produce deterministic outputs.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Record execution details.
+- Avoid modifying unrelated repository objects.
+
+---
+
+# Service Architecture
+
+A service SHOULD consist of:
+
+- Public interface
+- Configuration
+- Core processing logic
+- Validation
+- Error handling
+- Logging
+- Reporting
+
+Implementation details SHOULD remain internal.
+
+---
+
+# Service Lifecycle
+
+Every service execution SHOULD follow this sequence:
+
+1. Receive request.
+2. Validate inputs.
+3. Initialize execution context.
+4. Perform processing.
+5. Validate outputs.
+6. Record execution report.
+7. Return results.
+
+---
+
+# Inputs
+
+Service inputs SHOULD:
+
+- Conform to repository schemas.
+- Include required identifiers.
+- Preserve provenance information.
+- Be validated before processing.
+
+Invalid inputs SHALL generate explicit errors.
+
+---
+
+# Outputs
+
+Service outputs SHALL:
+
+- Conform to approved schemas.
+- Preserve identifiers.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Record execution metadata.
+
+Outputs SHALL be deterministic.
+
+---
+
+# Configuration
+
+Services SHOULD separate configuration from implementation.
+
+Configuration MAY include:
+
+- Processing options
+- Feature flags
+- Resource limits
+- Logging levels
+
+Configuration SHALL NOT alter repository governance.
+
+---
+
+# Error Handling
+
+Services SHALL classify errors as:
+
+- Validation Error
+- Processing Error
+- Dependency Error
+- Configuration Error
+- Internal Error
+
+Errors SHALL include sufficient diagnostic information for investigation.
+
+---
+
+# Logging
+
+Services SHOULD log:
+
+- Service name
+- Version
+- Execution start
+- Execution end
+- Duration
+- Warnings
+- Errors
+- Output summary
+
+Logs SHOULD support operational monitoring without replacing repository artifacts.
+
+---
+
+# Execution Reports
+
+Each execution SHOULD generate a report containing:
+
+- Service ID
+- Service version
+- Request identifier
+- Timestamp
+- Processing duration
+- Result status
+- Diagnostics
+- Output summary
+
+Execution reports SHALL support auditing and troubleshooting.
+
+---
+
+# Testing Requirements
+
+Every service SHOULD include:
+
+- Unit tests
+- Contract tests
+- Integration tests
+- Failure tests
+- Regression tests
+
+Tests SHOULD demonstrate compliance with the governing specification.
+
+---
+
+# Dependencies
+
+Services SHOULD:
+
+- Minimize dependencies.
+- Declare all external dependencies.
+- Fail gracefully when dependencies are unavailable.
+- Avoid circular service relationships.
+
+---
+
+# Extensibility
+
+New services SHOULD:
+
+- Implement existing contracts where possible.
+- Reuse shared components.
+- Avoid duplicating functionality.
+- Maintain backward compatibility unless governed otherwise.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Services are the workers of the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Specifications define what must happen.
+
+Services perform the work.
+
+By remaining modular, deterministic, and contract-driven, services enable the repository to evolve without compromising its constitutional foundation.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
