+# Validation Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Validation Specification defines the required checks performed on every ingested artifact before it proceeds through the ingestion pipeline.
+
+Validation ensures structural integrity, completeness, and specification compliance.
+
+---
+
+# Validation Principles
+
+- Validation is deterministic.
+- Validation preserves evidence.
+- Validation never modifies source artifacts.
+- Validation produces explicit results.
+- Validation failures are recoverable.
+
+---
+
+# Validation Levels
+
+## Level 1 — Artifact Integrity
+
+Verify:
+
+- Artifact exists.
+- Artifact ID assigned.
+- Source preserved.
+- Metadata present.
+
+---
+
+## Level 2 — Provenance
+
+Verify:
+
+- Provenance record exists.
+- Parent relationships recorded.
+- Import information complete.
+- Processing history initialized.
+
+---
+
+## Level 3 — Structure
+
+Verify:
+
+- Structural parsing completed.
+- Sections identified.
+- Assets extracted.
+- References captured.
+
+---
+
+## Level 4 — Queue Candidates
+
+Verify:
+
+- Queue candidate generation completed.
+- Queue records contain required metadata.
+- Queue assignments reference valid artifact IDs.
+
+---
+
+## Level 5 — Specification Compliance
+
+Verify compliance with:
+
+- Artifact Schema
+- Conversation Schema (if applicable)
+- Queue Specification
+- Provenance Specification
+- Output Package Specification
+
+---
+
+# Validation Results
+
+Each validation SHALL produce:
+
+- Validation ID
+- Artifact ID
+- Timestamp
+- Validator Version
+- Result
+- Findings
+
+---
+
+# Result States
+
+Possible results:
+
+- Pass
+- Pass with Warnings
+- Needs Review
+- Failed
+
+---
+
+# Failure Handling
+
+Validation failures SHALL:
+
+- Record all findings.
+- Preserve partial work.
+- Never discard evidence.
+- Prevent promotion until resolved.
+
+---
+
+# Warning Conditions
+
+Warnings MAY include:
+
+- Missing optional metadata.
+- Unresolved references.
+- Unknown asset types.
+- Unsupported formatting.
+
+Warnings SHALL NOT prevent ingestion.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Trail
+
+Every validation SHALL be recorded in the artifact's provenance history.
+
+Validation records SHALL be immutable.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Validation answers one question:
+
+"Does this artifact conform to the repository specifications?"
+
+It does not answer:
+
+"Is this artifact correct?"
+
+Quality assessment belongs to downstream review services.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
