+# Workflow Audit Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Workflow Audit Specification defines the canonical framework for recording, preserving, and analyzing workflow execution history throughout the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Auditing provides permanent institutional evidence of workflow activity, governance decisions, execution outcomes, and operational accountability.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Audit records are immutable.
+- Audit records preserve provenance.
+- Auditing is comprehensive.
+- Audit data is independently verifiable.
+- Audit history is permanently searchable.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+This specification applies to:
+
+- Workflow Definitions
+- Workflow Executions
+- Workflow Governance
+- Workflow Recovery
+- Workflow Replay
+- Workflow Versioning
+- Administrative Operations
+
+Every workflow-related operation SHALL be auditable.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Definition
+
+An audit record is an immutable record describing a workflow-related event, decision, state transition, or administrative action.
+
+Audit records SHALL become part of the permanent institutional history of the repository.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Objectives
+
+Workflow auditing SHALL provide:
+
+- Accountability
+- Traceability
+- Compliance support
+- Operational diagnostics
+- Historical reconstruction
+- Governance verification
+
+---
+
+# Audit Record Schema
+
+Every audit record SHALL contain:
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| Audit ID | Yes | Unique audit identifier |
+| Timestamp | Yes | Time of recorded activity |
+| Workflow ID | Yes | Associated workflow |
+| Execution ID | No | Associated execution, if applicable |
+| Correlation ID | Yes | Workflow correlation identifier |
+| Event Type | Yes | Recorded activity classification |
+| Actor | Yes | Responsible user, service, or system |
+| Action | Yes | Performed operation |
+| Target | Yes | Affected repository object |
+| Outcome | Yes | Result of the operation |
+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
+| Metadata | No | Supplemental audit information |
+
+---
+
+# Audit Identifier
+
+Audit IDs SHALL:
+
+- Be globally unique.
+- Never be reused.
+- Remain immutable.
+- Support repository indexing.
+
+---
+
+# Auditable Events
+
+The following SHALL generate audit records:
+
+- Workflow creation
+- Workflow modification
+- Workflow approval
+- Workflow publication
+- Workflow execution
+- Workflow suspension
+- Workflow recovery
+- Workflow replay
+- Workflow cancellation
+- Workflow completion
+- Workflow archival
+- Administrative override
+
+Additional events MAY be audited according to governance policy.
+
+---
+
+# Governance Auditing
+
+Governance actions SHALL record:
+
+- Reviewer
+- Approver
+- Decision
+- Timestamp
+- Supporting rationale
+- Related change request
+
+Governance records SHALL remain permanently available.
+
+---
+
+# Execution Auditing
+
+Workflow execution SHALL record:
+
+- Execution start
+- Step completion
+- Validation results
+- State transitions
+- Service interactions
+- Completion status
+- Failure diagnostics
+
+Execution auditing SHALL enable complete workflow reconstruction.
+
+---
+
+# Administrative Auditing
+
+Administrative actions SHALL include:
+
+- Configuration changes
+- Workflow activation
+- Workflow deactivation
+- Policy modifications
+- Exception approvals
+- Repository maintenance
+
+Administrative operations SHALL require attribution.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Integrity
+
+Audit records SHALL:
+
+- Remain immutable.
+- Preserve chronological ordering.
+- Maintain provenance continuity.
+- Support integrity verification.
+
+Modification of audit records SHALL NOT be permitted.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Retention
+
+Audit records SHALL follow repository retention policies.
+
+Retention SHALL preserve:
+
+- Historical executions
+- Governance history
+- Compliance evidence
+- Provenance continuity
+
+Audit retention SHALL prioritize institutional memory.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Search
+
+Audit services SHOULD support searching by:
+
+- Audit ID
+- Workflow ID
+- Execution ID
+- Correlation ID
+- Event Type
+- Actor
+- Timestamp
+- Outcome
+
+Search capabilities SHALL support operational analysis and compliance activities.
+
+---
+
+# Monitoring
+
+Audit services SHOULD expose:
+
+- Total audit records
+- Daily audit volume
+- Failed audit writes
+- Audit storage utilization
+- Search performance
+- Audit integrity verification status
+
+Monitoring SHALL ensure audit reliability.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Audit validation SHALL verify:
+
+- Identifier uniqueness
+- Required metadata
+- Provenance continuity
+- Timestamp validity
+- Workflow references
+- Repository consistency
+
+Invalid audit records SHALL be rejected.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Integration
+
+Workflow Auditing integrates with:
+
+- Workflow Governance
+- Workflow Execution
+- Workflow Recovery
+- Workflow Replay
+- Workflow Versioning
+- Event Processing
+- Provenance
+- Repository Indexes
+- Observability
+
+Audit operations SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Every workflow represents an institutional process.
+
+Every institutional process deserves an institutional memory.
+
+Workflow auditing transforms operational activity into durable evidence, ensuring that every decision, execution, and governance action can be reconstructed, verified, and understood long after the original execution has completed.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
