+# Workflow Context Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Workflow Context Specification defines the canonical execution context shared by every workflow within the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Workflow Context provides the information necessary for coordinated execution.
+
+It SHALL remain separate from workflow logic.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Context is immutable wherever practical.
+- Context is shared.
+- Context preserves provenance.
+- Context is reproducible.
+- Context is independently validatable.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+Workflow Context applies to:
+
+- Workflow Orchestration
+- Workflow Execution
+- Services
+- Parsers
+- Validation
+- Repository Mapping
+- Publication
+- Automation
+
+Every participating component SHALL receive the same workflow context.
+
+---
+
+# Canonical Workflow Context
+
+Every workflow context SHALL contain:
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| Workflow ID | Yes | Workflow definition identifier |
+| Execution ID | Yes | Current execution identifier |
+| Correlation ID | Yes | Shared workflow correlation identifier |
+| Workflow Version | Yes | Workflow definition version |
+| Execution State | Yes | Current workflow state |
+| Artifact ID | Yes | Primary repository artifact |
+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance chain reference |
+| Repository Context | Yes | Repository execution environment |
+| Start Timestamp | Yes | Workflow start time |
+| Execution Metadata | No | Additional execution information |
+| Execution Parameters | No | Runtime parameters |
+| Parent Workflow ID | No | Parent workflow reference |
+
+---
+
+# Workflow Identifier
+
+Workflow ID SHALL reference an approved Workflow Definition.
+
+Workflow IDs SHALL remain constant throughout execution.
+
+---
+
+# Execution Identifier
+
+Execution IDs SHALL uniquely identify individual workflow executions.
+
+Multiple executions MAY exist for the same Workflow ID.
+
+Execution IDs SHALL never be reused.
+
+---
+
+# Correlation Identifier
+
+All services participating in the same workflow SHALL use the same Correlation ID.
+
+Correlation SHALL enable reconstruction of complete execution history.
+
+---
+
+# Execution State
+
+Execution State SHALL conform to the Workflow State Machine Specification.
+
+Only valid state transitions SHALL occur.
+
+---
+
+# Artifact Identifier
+
+Every workflow SHALL identify its primary repository artifact.
+
+Additional artifacts MAY be referenced through execution metadata.
+
+---
+
+# Provenance
+
+Workflow Context SHALL reference the active Provenance Record.
+
+All derived repository objects SHALL extend this provenance chain.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Context
+
+Repository Context SHOULD identify:
+
+- Repository version
+- Repository branch
+- Repository configuration
+- Execution environment
+
+Repository Context SHALL support reproducibility.
+
+---
+
+# Execution Metadata
+
+Execution Metadata MAY include:
+
+- Request origin
+- Initiating user or service
+- Processing statistics
+- Resource allocations
+- Execution notes
+
+Metadata SHALL NOT alter workflow behavior.
+
+---
+
+# Execution Parameters
+
+Execution Parameters MAY define:
+
+- Processing options
+- Feature flags
+- Operational limits
+- Retry behavior
+
+Parameters SHALL remain explicit.
+
+---
+
+# Parent Workflow
+
+Nested workflows MAY reference a Parent Workflow ID.
+
+Parent-child relationships SHALL remain acyclic.
+
+---
+
+# Context Propagation
+
+Workflow Context SHALL propagate unchanged between participating services unless explicitly extended according to approved schemas.
+
+Services SHALL NOT remove existing context fields.
+
+---
+
+# Context Validation
+
+Workflow Context SHALL validate:
+
+- Required identifiers
+- Workflow definition
+- Execution state
+- Provenance reference
+- Repository context
+- Schema version
+
+Invalid context SHALL prevent workflow execution.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Integration
+
+Workflow Context integrates with:
+
+- Workflow Definition Schema
+- Workflow Execution
+- Workflow State Machine
+- Event Model
+- Provenance
+- Validation
+- Repository Indexes
+
+Workflow Context SHALL preserve repository consistency throughout execution.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+A workflow is more than a sequence of steps.
+
+It is a shared execution environment.
+
+Workflow Context provides the common frame of reference that allows independent services to cooperate while preserving provenance, determinism, and institutional memory.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
