+# Workflow Orchestration Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1
+**Status:** Draft
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Workflow Orchestration Specification defines how repository workflows are coordinated across independent services.
+
+Orchestration manages execution.
+
+Services perform work.
+
+Events communicate outcomes.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Workflows are deterministic.
+- Services remain loosely coupled.
+- Orchestration preserves provenance.
+- Execution is observable.
+- Recovery is supported.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+This specification applies to:
+
+- Artifact ingestion workflows
+- Validation workflows
+- Repository mapping workflows
+- Governance workflows
+- Publication workflows
+- Automation workflows
+
+---
+
+# Workflow Definition
+
+A workflow is an ordered sequence of coordinated service executions that together accomplish a repository objective.
+
+Each workflow SHALL possess:
+
+- Workflow ID
+- Workflow Type
+- Current State
+- Correlation ID
+- Start Time
+- End Time
+- Execution History
+
+---
+
+# Workflow States
+
+Every workflow SHALL exist in one of the following states:
+
+- Created
+- Waiting
+- Running
+- Suspended
+- Completed
+- Failed
+- Cancelled
+- Archived
+
+State transitions SHALL be recorded.
+
+---
+
+# Workflow Lifecycle
+
+A typical workflow progresses through:
+
+1. Created
+2. Initialized
+3. Running
+4. Awaiting Dependencies
+5. Continuing Execution
+6. Completed
+
+Alternative paths include:
+
+- Failed
+- Cancelled
+- Suspended
+
+---
+
+# Workflow Coordinator
+
+The orchestration layer SHALL:
+
+- Initialize workflows.
+- Schedule service execution.
+- Monitor workflow progress.
+- Record execution history.
+- Coordinate recovery.
+- Detect completion.
+
+The coordinator SHALL NOT perform service-specific business logic.
+
+---
+
+# Service Coordination
+
+Services participating in workflows SHALL:
+
+- Advertise supported contracts.
+- Accept workflow context.
+- Return execution results.
+- Publish completion events.
+
+Services SHALL remain independently executable.
+
+---
+
+# Dependency Management
+
+Workflow steps MAY declare dependencies.
+
+Dependencies SHALL identify:
+
+- Required predecessor
+- Dependency type
+- Completion condition
+
+Execution SHALL wait until dependencies are satisfied.
+
+---
+
+# Parallel Execution
+
+Independent workflow steps MAY execute concurrently.
+
+Parallel execution SHALL preserve:
+
+- Deterministic outcomes
+- Provenance
+- Correlation
+- Execution history
+
+Parallel execution SHALL NOT violate service contracts.
+
+---
+
+# Workflow Context
+
+Workflow context SHOULD include:
+
+- Workflow ID
+- Correlation ID
+- Artifact ID
+- Repository Context
+- Execution Parameters
+- Provenance Reference
+
+Context SHALL remain consistent throughout execution.
+
+---
+
+# Failure Handling
+
+Workflow failures SHALL:
+
+- Preserve completed work.
+- Record failure details.
+- Preserve execution history.
+- Support recovery.
+
+Failure SHALL NOT corrupt repository state.
+
+---
+
+# Recovery
+
+Recoverable workflows MAY resume from the most recent successful checkpoint.
+
+Recovery SHALL:
+
+- Preserve Workflow ID.
+- Preserve Correlation ID.
+- Preserve completed stages.
+- Record recovery events.
+
+Recovery SHALL NOT repeat completed work unnecessarily.
+
+---
+
+# Cancellation
+
+Cancelled workflows SHALL:
+
+- Record cancellation time.
+- Record cancellation reason.
+- Preserve completed outputs.
+- Publish cancellation events.
+
+Cancellation SHALL remain part of workflow history.
+
+---
+
+# Monitoring
+
+Workflow orchestration SHOULD expose:
+
+- Active workflows
+- Workflow duration
+- Failure count
+- Success rate
+- Recovery count
+- Queue depth
+- Pending dependencies
+
+Operational monitoring SHALL support diagnosis.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Workflow execution SHALL verify:
+
+- Workflow definition
+- Service compatibility
+- Dependency satisfaction
+- Context validity
+- State transition validity
+
+Invalid workflows SHALL be rejected before execution.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Integration
+
+Workflow orchestration integrates with:
+
+- Event Processing
+- Event Routing
+- Lifecycle Management
+- Validation
+- Observability
+- Security
+- Repository Indexes
+
+Workflow execution SHALL preserve repository integrity.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Services perform individual tasks.
+
+Workflows transform those tasks into coordinated capability.
+
+Orchestration enables the Repository Ingestion Framework to evolve as a collection of independent services while behaving as a coherent institutional system.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
