+# Workflow Service Communication Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Workflow Service Communication Specification defines the canonical architecture governing communication between services participating in the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+Communication establishes standardized, deterministic, and auditable exchanges of requests, responses, events, and execution context while preserving service autonomy, repository integrity, and institutional governance.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- Communication is contract-driven.
+- Communication is deterministic.
+- Communication is version-aware.
+- Communication is observable.
+- Communication preserves provenance.
+- Communication is implementation-independent.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+This specification applies to:
+
+- Workflow Services
+- Parser Services
+- Validation Services
+- Mapping Services
+- Repository Services
+- Publication Services
+- Governance Services
+- Utility Services
+- Administrative Services
+
+---
+
+# Communication Definition
+
+Service Communication is the governed exchange of information between two or more services through approved communication mechanisms and service contracts.
+
+Communication SHALL be explicit, validated, and independently auditable.
+
+---
+
+# Communication Objectives
+
+Service communication SHALL provide:
+
+- Reliable information exchange
+- Deterministic service interaction
+- Consistent context propagation
+- Version compatibility
+- Failure transparency
+- Governance compliance
+
+---
+
+# Canonical Communication Schema
+
+Every communication definition SHALL contain:
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| Communication ID | Yes | Unique communication identifier |
+| Communication Name | Yes | Human-readable name |
+| Communication Version | Yes | Semantic version |
+| Sender Service | Yes | Originating service |
+| Receiver Service | Yes | Destination service |
+| Communication Type | Yes | Communication pattern |
+| Contract Reference | Yes | Governing service contract |
+| Message Schema | Yes | Message definition |
+| Reliability Policy | Yes | Delivery guarantees |
+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
+| Metadata | No | Supplemental communication information |
+
+---
+
+# Communication Types
+
+Supported communication types include:
+
+- Request-Response
+- Event Publication
+- Event Subscription
+- Command
+- Notification
+- Broadcast
+- Query
+- Streaming
+- Administrative Communication
+
+Additional communication types MAY be introduced through governance.
+
+---
+
+# Communication Patterns
+
+Communication SHALL support the following patterns:
+
+- Synchronous
+- Asynchronous
+- One-to-One
+- One-to-Many
+- Many-to-One
+- Publish-Subscribe
+- Request-Reply
+
+Each communication SHALL explicitly declare its pattern.
+
+---
+
+# Service Identification
+
+Every communication SHALL identify:
+
+- Sender Service ID
+- Receiver Service ID
+- Service Version
+- Capability Reference
+- Contract Version
+
+Identity SHALL be validated before communication begins.
+
+---
+
+# Message Structure
+
+Every message SHALL include:
+
+- Message ID
+- Correlation ID
+- Workflow ID
+- Execution ID
+- Timestamp
+- Sender
+- Receiver
+- Payload
+- Metadata
+- Provenance Reference
+
+Messages SHALL conform to approved schemas.
+
+---
+
+# Context Propagation
+
+Communication SHALL preserve execution context.
+
+Context SHALL include:
+
+- Workflow Identifier
+- Execution Identifier
+- Correlation Identifier
+- Repository Context
+- Security Context
+- Provenance Identifier
+- Configuration Context
+
+Context SHALL remain unchanged unless explicitly modified through governance-approved rules.
+
+---
+
+# Contract Compliance
+
+Every communication SHALL comply with:
+
+- Service Contract
+- Capability Definition
+- Version Compatibility
+- Message Schema
+- Repository Policies
+
+Contract violations SHALL prevent message processing.
+
+---
+
+# Reliability Policy
+
+Communication reliability SHALL define:
+
+- Delivery guarantees
+- Retry behavior
+- Timeout policy
+- Duplicate handling
+- Ordering guarantees
+- Failure reporting
+
+Reliability policies SHALL be deterministic.
+
+---
+
+# Message Ordering
+
+Where ordering is required, communication SHALL preserve:
+
+- Workflow order
+- Dependency order
+- Event sequence
+- Causal relationships
+- Checkpoint consistency
+
+Ordering guarantees SHALL be explicitly declared.
+
+---
+
+# Communication Failures
+
+Communication SHALL detect and classify:
+
+- Delivery failure
+- Timeout
+- Validation failure
+- Authentication failure
+- Authorization failure
+- Schema incompatibility
+- Dependency failure
+- Transport failure
+
+Failures SHALL generate operational events.
+
+---
+
+# Security
+
+Communication SHALL enforce:
+
+- Authentication
+- Authorization
+- Integrity verification
+- Confidentiality where required
+- Non-repudiation
+- Audit recording
+
+Unauthorized communication SHALL be rejected.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Communication validation SHALL verify:
+
+- Service identity
+- Contract compatibility
+- Message schema
+- Version compatibility
+- Security compliance
+- Repository connectivity
+
+Validation SHALL complete before message acceptance.
+
+---
+
+# Communication Events
+
+Communication services SHALL publish events including:
+
+- Communication Initiated
+- Message Sent
+- Message Received
+- Message Validated
+- Message Rejected
+- Communication Failed
+- Retry Initiated
+- Communication Completed
+
+Events SHALL conform to the Event Model Specification.
+
+---
+
+# Audit Requirements
+
+Communication activities SHALL record:
+
+- Communication ID
+- Sender Service
+- Receiver Service
+- Message ID
+- Contract Version
+- Validation Result
+- Timestamp
+- Provenance Reference
+
+Audit records SHALL remain immutable.
+
+---
+
+# Monitoring
+
+Communication monitoring SHOULD expose:
+
+- Messages transmitted
+- Messages received
+- Communication latency
+- Validation failures
+- Retry frequency
+- Timeout frequency
+- Communication errors
+- Throughput
+
+Monitoring SHALL support operational governance and performance optimization.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Integration
+
+Workflow Service Communication integrates with:
+
+- Workflow Service Contracts
+- Workflow Service Registry
+- Workflow Service Discovery
+- Workflow Service Dependencies
+- Workflow Service Coordination
+- Workflow Service Composition
+- Workflow Execution
+- Event Processing
+- Observability
+- Repository Indexes
+
+Communication SHALL preserve repository integrity, deterministic execution, and institutional accountability.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Communication is the architectural fabric that connects independent services into cohesive workflows.
+
+By governing communication through explicit contracts, validated message schemas, deterministic interaction patterns, and comprehensive auditability, the Repository Ingestion Framework enables reliable collaboration while maintaining loose coupling, reproducibility, and long-term architectural sustainability.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
\ No newline at end of file
