+# Workflow Service Registry Specification
+
+**Version:** 0.1  
+**Status:** Draft  
+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+The Workflow Service Registry Specification defines the canonical registry for discovering, identifying, validating, and governing workflow services participating in the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+The Service Registry provides a single authoritative catalog of all approved services and their capabilities.
+
+---
+
+# Design Principles
+
+- The registry is authoritative.
+- Registry entries are immutable by version.
+- Service discovery is deterministic.
+- Registry metadata preserves provenance.
+- Service capabilities are explicitly declared.
+- Registry operations are independently auditable.
+
+---
+
+# Scope
+
+This specification applies to:
+
+- Workflow Services
+- Parser Services
+- Validation Services
+- Asset Services
+- Mapping Services
+- Publication Services
+- Governance Services
+- Utility Services
+- Administrative Services
+
+---
+
+# Registry Definition
+
+The Service Registry is the canonical repository of approved workflow services.
+
+Every service participating in workflow execution SHALL possess a registry entry.
+
+---
+
+# Registry Objectives
+
+The registry SHALL provide:
+
+- Service discovery
+- Service identification
+- Capability declaration
+- Version management
+- Compatibility tracking
+- Governance support
+
+---
+
+# Canonical Registry Schema
+
+Every registry entry SHALL contain:
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| Registry ID | Yes | Unique registry identifier |
+| Service ID | Yes | Unique service identifier |
+| Service Name | Yes | Human-readable service name |
+| Service Version | Yes | Semantic version |
+| Service Type | Yes | Functional classification |
+| Status | Yes | Lifecycle status |
+| Owner | Yes | Responsible owner |
+| Supported Contracts | Yes | Implemented service contracts |
+| Supported Workflow Types | Yes | Compatible workflow categories |
+| Supported Schema Versions | Yes | Supported schemas |
+| Dependencies | No | Required external services |
+| Endpoint Reference | No | Service endpoint reference |
+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
+| Metadata | No | Supplemental information |
+
+---
+
+# Registry Identifier
+
+Registry identifiers SHALL:
+
+- Be globally unique.
+- Never be reused.
+- Remain immutable.
+- Support repository indexing.
+
+Example:
+
+SR-000001
+
+---
+
+# Service Lifecycle
+
+Registry entries SHALL progress through:
+
+Draft
+
+↓
+
+Review
+
+↓
+
+Approved
+
+↓
+
+Registered
+
+↓
+
+Active
+
+↓
+
+Deprecated
+
+↓
+
+Archived
+
+Lifecycle changes SHALL be governed.
+
+---
+
+# Service Classification
+
+Registry classifications MAY include:
+
+- Parser
+- Validation
+- Mapping
+- Publication
+- Governance
+- Event
+- Repository
+- Monitoring
+- Utility
+- Administrative
+
+Additional classifications MAY be introduced through governance.
+
+---
+
+# Capability Declaration
+
+Every registered service SHALL declare:
+
+- Supported operations
+- Supported contracts
+- Accepted inputs
+- Produced outputs
+- Published events
+- Supported workflow stages
+
+Capabilities SHALL remain versioned.
+
+---
+
+# Dependency Declaration
+
+Services MAY declare dependencies upon:
+
+- Other services
+- Repository components
+- External systems
+- Approved schemas
+- Event channels
+
+Dependency relationships SHALL remain acyclic wherever practical.
+
+---
+
+# Compatibility
+
+Registry entries SHALL document compatibility with:
+
+- Workflow Definitions
+- Workflow Versions
+- Service Contracts
+- Event Schemas
+- Repository Versions
+- API Versions
+
+Compatibility SHALL be explicitly maintained.
+
+---
+
+# Discovery
+
+Registry services SHOULD support discovery by:
+
+- Service ID
+- Service Name
+- Service Type
+- Capability
+- Workflow Type
+- Version
+- Owner
+- Status
+
+Discovery SHALL return only approved registry metadata.
+
+---
+
+# Registration
+
+New service registration SHALL require:
+
+- Approved service contract
+- Successful validation
+- Governance approval
+- Compatibility verification
+- Provenance assignment
+
+Unapproved services SHALL NOT participate in production workflows.
+
+---
+
+# Deregistration
+
+Services SHALL only be deregistered through approved governance procedures.
+
+Deregistration SHALL:
+
+- Preserve historical registry records.
+- Preserve provenance.
+- Preserve execution history.
+- Archive registry metadata.
+
+Historical registry entries SHALL remain searchable.
+
+---
+
+# Validation
+
+Registry validation SHALL verify:
+
+- Identifier uniqueness
+- Contract compatibility
+- Version consistency
+- Capability declarations
+- Dependency integrity
+- Governance approval
+
+Invalid registry entries SHALL NOT become Active.
+
+---
+
+# Monitoring
+
+Registry services SHOULD expose:
+
+- Registered services
+- Active services
+- Deprecated services
+- Registration requests
+- Validation failures
+- Compatibility issues
+- Discovery requests
+
+Monitoring SHALL support repository operations.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Integration
+
+Workflow Service Registry integrates with:
+
+- Workflow Service Contracts
+- Workflow Definition Schema
+- Workflow Execution
+- Workflow API
+- Workflow Governance
+- Repository Indexes
+- Event Processing
+- Observability
+
+Registry operations SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
+
+---
+
+# Design Philosophy
+
+Services are the operational building blocks of workflow execution.
+
+The Service Registry transforms a collection of independent implementations into a governed institutional ecosystem by providing a single authoritative source of truth for service identity, capability, compatibility, and lifecycle.
+
+This authoritative registry enables deterministic orchestration, controlled evolution, and long-term maintainability across the Repository Ingestion Framework.
+
+---
+
+End of Specification.
