+# DE - Repository Map
+Status: Canonical
+Revision: 1.0
+Authority: The Difference Engine
+Repository Root: DifferenceEngine/
+
+---
+
+# Purpose
+
+This document defines the purpose, authority, ownership, lifecycle, and relationships of every top-level component of The Difference Engine repository.
+
+The repository is the institutional memory and implementation substrate of The Difference Engine.
+
+This document is the authoritative map of the repository.
+
+The repository tree defines *where* artifacts reside.
+
+This document defines *why* they reside there.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Principles
+
+The repository SHALL be:
+
+- Repository-first.
+- Constitution-governed.
+- Deterministic.
+- Provenance-preserving.
+- Recoverable.
+- Canonical.
+- Self-documenting.
+- Ingestion-ready.
+
+---
+
+# Repository Lifecycle
+
+Conversation
+
+↓
+
+Evidence
+
+↓
+
+Working Artifact
+
+↓
+
+DE - TOPIC
+
+↓
+
+Canonical Artifact
+
+↓
+
+Memory Palace
+
+Nothing is discarded.
+
+Everything has a lifecycle.
+
+---
+
+# Top-Level Directories
+
+## 00_INDEX
+
+Purpose
+
+Repository navigation.
+
+Authority
+
+Repository.
+
+Contains
+
+Master indexes.
+
+Artifact registry.
+
+Cross references.
+
+Search indexes.
+
+Eventually generated by the ingester.
+
+---
+
+## 00_FOUNDATION
+
+Purpose
+
+Defines why The Difference Engine exists.
+
+Contains
+
+Mission
+
+Vision
+
+Roadmap
+
+Current Program
+
+Institution History
+
+Foundation Summits
+
+---
+
+## 01_CONSTITUTION
+
+Purpose
+
+Defines institutional authority.
+
+Contains
+
+Constitution
+
+Governance
+
+Authorities
+
+Office Specifications
+
+Branch Charters
+
+Ratifications
+
+Only ratified governance belongs here.
+
+---
+
+## 02_PROJECT
+
+Purpose
+
+Defines the ChatGPT Project itself.
+
+Contains
+
+DE - Project.md
+
+Project Instructions
+
+Project Sources
+
+Initialization
+
+Recovery
+
+Configuration
+
+This governs the Project—not the institution.
+
+---
+
+## 03_REPOSITORY
+
+Purpose
+
+Defines repository governance.
+
+Contains
+
+Repository standards.
+
+Topology.
+
+Naming.
+
+Promotion.
+
+Lifecycle.
+
+Repository Control.
+
+---
+
+## 04_OPERATIONS
+
+Purpose
+
+Current engineering execution.
+
+Contains
+
+Work Packages.
+
+Queues.
+
+Milestones.
+
+Session closeouts.
+
+Current operational state.
+
+This directory changes most frequently.
+
+---
+
+## 05_OFFICES
