-+# Information Architecture
-+
-+Document ID: INFO-0001
-+Version: 0.1.0
-+Status: Draft
-+Owner:
-+Created:
-+Last Updated:
-+Authority: Governance
-+Supersedes:
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+Define the conceptual organization of the repository and establish where different types of knowledge belong.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Principles
-+
-+- Every document should have a clear purpose.
-+- Every document should have one canonical location.
-+- Documents should be organized by function rather than chronology.
-+- Governance defines rules.
-+- Architecture describes structure.
-+- Specifications define requirements.
-+- Decisions capture rationale.
-+- Publications communicate completed work.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Knowledge Types
-+
-+## Governance (GOV)
-+
-+Defines repository policies, standards, and rules.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Architecture (ARC)
-+
-+Describes how systems are organized and relate to one another.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Specifications (SPEC)
-+
-+Describe required behavior, interfaces, or expectations.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Architecture Decision Records (ADR)
-+
-+Capture significant decisions, their context, alternatives, and consequences.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Publications (PUB)
-+
-+Finished documents intended for sharing or long-term reference.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Information Flow
-+
-+Ideas
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Research
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Discussion
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Decision
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Specification
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Implementation
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Publication
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Stewardship
-+
-+The repository exists to reduce ambiguity, preserve reasoning, and improve discoverability over time.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# References
-+
-+- Repository README
-+- FILE_NAMING.md
-+- DOCUMENT_METADATA.md
-+- WRITING_GUIDELINES.md
