-+# Document Metadata Standard
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+This document defines the standard metadata used by canonical ADE repository documents.
-+
-+A consistent metadata block improves discoverability, governance, automation, and long-term stewardship.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Standard Metadata
-+
-+| Field | Required | Purpose |
-+|--------|:--------:|---------|
-+| Document ID | Yes | Permanent identifier for the document. |
-+| Version | Yes | Current revision number. |
-+| Status | Yes | Draft, Active, Archived, or Superseded. |
-+| Owner | Yes | Responsible steward or team. |
-+| Created | Yes | Original creation date. |
-+| Last Updated | Yes | Most recent revision date. |
-+| Authority | Yes | Governing domain of the document. |
-+| Supersedes | Yes | Previous document replaced, if any. |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Status Values
-+
-+- Draft
-+- Active
-+- Archived
-+- Superseded
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Authority Values
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Governance
-+- Architecture
-+- Stewardship
-+- Knowledge
-+- Publication
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Notes
-+
-+Templates should include the standard metadata block.
-+
-+Automation scripts may populate these fields automatically in the future.
