-+# Markdown Style Guide
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+This document defines the Markdown formatting conventions used throughout the ADE repository.
-+
-+Consistency improves readability and simplifies automation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Headings
-+
-+Use ATX headings.
-+
-+Example:
-+
-+# Level 1
-+
-+## Level 2
-+
-+### Level 3
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Lists
-+
-+Use hyphens (`-`) for unordered lists.
-+
-+Use numbered lists only when sequence matters.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Tables
-+
-+Use Markdown tables when presenting structured information.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Code
-+
-+Wrap commands, file names, and code in fenced code blocks or inline backticks as appropriate.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Spacing
-+
-+Use one blank line between sections.
-+
-+Avoid unnecessary blank lines.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Line Length
-+
-+Wrap naturally for readability.
-+
-+Do not force hard line limits.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# File Format
-+
-+- UTF-8 encoding
-+- Unix line endings when practical
-+- `.md` file extension
