-+# Writing Guidelines
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+These guidelines promote clarity, consistency, and long-term maintainability across the ADE repository.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Principles
-+
-+- Write for future readers.
-+- Prefer clarity over cleverness.
-+- Prefer precision over verbosity.
-+- State observations before interpretations.
-+- Define terms before using them extensively.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Style
-+
-+- Prefer active voice.
-+- Use concise sentences.
-+- Avoid unnecessary jargon.
-+- Explain abbreviations on first use.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Stewardship
-+
-+Repository documents should reduce ambiguity rather than increase it.
-+
-+When revising a document, improve understanding without altering historical evidence.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Revision Philosophy
-+
-+Documentation is expected to evolve.
-+
-+Changing one's understanding in light of better evidence is a strength, not a weakness.
