-+# Canonical Promotion Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Canonical Promotion Specification defines the process by which reviewed artifacts become canonical repository knowledge.
-+
-+Promotion is a governance activity.
-+
-+Promotion SHALL preserve provenance, lineage, and repository history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Promotion Principles
-+
-+- Promotion is intentional.
-+- Promotion is review-driven.
-+- Promotion never destroys evidence.
-+- Promotion preserves history.
-+- Promotion creates canonical knowledge.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Promotion Eligibility
-+
-+An artifact MAY be considered for promotion if it:
-+
-+- Successfully completed ingestion.
-+- Passed validation.
-+- Completed repository mapping.
-+- Retains complete provenance.
-+- Has been reviewed.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Promotion Inputs
-+
-+Promotion SHALL consider:
-+
-+- Artifact Record
-+- Validation Report
-+- Mapping Report
-+- Queue History
-+- Provenance Record
-+- Reviewer Decision
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Promotion Outputs
-+
-+Promotion SHALL produce:
-+
-+- Canonical Artifact
-+- Promotion Record
-+- Updated Repository Index
-+- Updated Lineage Records
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Review Requirements
-+
-+Promotion SHALL require review.
-+
-+Review MAY be performed by:
-+
-+- Human reviewer
-+- Future governance workflows
-+- Future approved automation
-+
-+Review authority SHALL be explicitly recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Promotion Record
-+
-+Every promotion SHALL record:
-+
-+- Promotion ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Reviewer
-+- Timestamp
-+- Destination
-+- Reason
-+- Version
-+
-+Promotion records are immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Versioning
-+
-+Promotion SHALL create a new canonical version.
-+
-+Previous canonical versions SHALL remain accessible.
-+
-+History SHALL NOT be destroyed.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Supersession
-+
-+When an artifact replaces another:
-+
-+- Previous artifact remains preserved.
-+- Supersession relationship is recorded.
-+- Repository indexes are updated.
-+- Provenance remains intact.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Rejection
-+
-+Artifacts not promoted SHALL remain repository artifacts.
-+
-+Rejection SHALL NOT delete evidence.
-+
-+Reasons for rejection SHALL be recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Rollback
-+
-+Canonical promotion MAY be reversed.
-+
-+Rollback SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve history.
-+- Record the rollback.
-+- Restore prior canonical state.
-+- Never remove provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication
-+
-+Promotion authorizes publication.
-+
-+Publication SHALL occur through the Publication Service.
-+
-+Promotion and publication are separate operations.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Evidence becomes knowledge through governance.
-+
-+Governance creates canonical knowledge.
-+
-+Canonical knowledge remains traceable to evidence.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
