-+# Configuration Management Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Configuration Management Specification defines how configuration information is created, organized, versioned, validated, and maintained within the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Configuration controls system behavior.
-+
-+Configuration SHALL NOT alter repository governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Configuration is explicit.
-+- Configuration is versioned.
-+- Configuration is reproducible.
-+- Configuration is validated.
-+- Configuration is separate from implementation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+Configuration management applies to:
-+
-+- Services
-+- Parsers
-+- Validation engines
-+- Repository mapping
-+- Queue generation
-+- Automation
-+- Operational infrastructure
-+
-+Repository artifacts themselves are NOT configuration.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Configuration Categories
-+
-+The repository SHALL recognize the following configuration categories:
-+
-+- System Configuration
-+- Service Configuration
-+- Parser Configuration
-+- Validation Configuration
-+- Logging Configuration
-+- Monitoring Configuration
-+- Deployment Configuration
-+
-+Additional categories MAY be introduced through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Configuration Files
-+
-+Configuration files SHOULD:
-+
-+- Be human-readable.
-+- Be version controlled.
-+- Follow approved schemas.
-+- Include documentation.
-+- Avoid implementation-specific assumptions.
-+
-+Recommended formats include:
-+
-+- YAML
-+- JSON
-+- TOML
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Configuration Metadata
-+
-+Every configuration SHALL include:
-+
-+- Configuration Identifier
-+- Version
-+- Owner
-+- Date Created
-+- Date Modified
-+- Description
-+
-+Metadata SHALL support traceability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Versioning
-+
-+Configuration versions SHALL be recorded independently from implementation versions.
-+
-+Configuration changes SHOULD reference:
-+
-+- Related specifications
-+- Related services
-+- Related schemas
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Configuration SHALL be validated before use.
-+
-+Validation SHOULD verify:
-+
-+- Required fields
-+- Supported values
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Dependency consistency
-+- Version compatibility
-+
-+Invalid configuration SHALL prevent execution.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Change Management
-+
-+Configuration changes SHOULD:
-+
-+- Be reviewed.
-+- Be documented.
-+- Be versioned.
-+- Preserve historical versions.
-+
-+Configuration history SHALL remain accessible.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Environment Separation
-+
-+Operational environments SHOULD maintain separate configurations for:
-+
-+- Development
-+- Testing
-+- Staging
-+- Production
-+
-+Environment-specific configuration SHALL NOT alter repository governance rules.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Secrets Management
-+
-+Sensitive information SHOULD NOT be stored directly within repository configuration.
-+
-+Sensitive information MAY include:
-+
-+- Authentication credentials
-+- API keys
-+- Access tokens
-+- Encryption keys
-+
-+Operational implementations SHOULD use dedicated secret management mechanisms.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Configuration Auditing
-+
-+Configuration history SHOULD record:
-+
-+- Change identifier
-+- Author
-+- Timestamp
-+- Description
-+- Previous version
-+- Current version
-+
-+Audit history SHALL be immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Recovery
-+
-+Repository operations SHOULD support:
-+
-+- Configuration backup
-+- Configuration restoration
-+- Version rollback
-+- Validation after recovery
-+
-+Recovery SHALL preserve configuration history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Configuration defines how the Repository Ingestion Framework operates.
-+
-+Specifications define what it must accomplish.
-+
-+By separating configuration from implementation, the repository remains adaptable while preserving constitutional consistency.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
