-+# Event Model Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Event Model Specification defines the canonical event system for the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Events communicate that something has occurred.
-+
-+Events describe facts.
-+
-+Events SHALL NOT perform work.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Events represent completed observations.
-+- Events are immutable.
-+- Events preserve chronology.
-+- Events preserve provenance.
-+- Events are append-only.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+The event model applies to:
-+
-+- Services
-+- Parsers
-+- Validation
-+- Repository Mapping
-+- Queue Management
-+- Governance
-+- Publication
-+- Operational Monitoring
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Definition
-+
-+An event is a timestamped record describing the occurrence of a repository activity.
-+
-+Events communicate state transitions without containing business logic.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Categories
-+
-+The Repository SHALL support the following event categories:
-+
-+- Intake Events
-+- Parser Events
-+- Asset Events
-+- Reference Events
-+- Validation Events
-+- Queue Events
-+- Lifecycle Events
-+- Governance Events
-+- Publication Events
-+- System Events
-+
-+Additional categories MAY be introduced through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Standard Event Structure
-+
-+Every event SHALL include:
-+
-+- Event ID
-+- Event Type
-+- Event Category
-+- Timestamp
-+- Source Component
-+- Subject Identifier
-+- Event Version
-+
-+Optional fields MAY include:
-+
-+- Parent Event ID
-+- Correlation ID
-+- Processing Duration
-+- Diagnostic Information
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Lifecycle
-+
-+Events SHALL progress through:
-+
-+1. Created
-+2. Recorded
-+3. Published
-+4. Archived
-+
-+Once recorded, events SHALL NOT be modified.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Ordering
-+
-+Events SHOULD preserve chronological order.
-+
-+Where strict ordering cannot be guaranteed, timestamps and correlation identifiers SHALL permit reconstruction of execution history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Correlation
-+
-+Related events SHOULD share a common Correlation ID.
-+
-+Correlation enables reconstruction of workflows spanning multiple services.
-+
-+Example:
-+
-+Artifact Intake
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Structural Parsing
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Asset Extraction
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Validation
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Publication
-+
-+Each event references the same Correlation ID.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Types
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+## Intake
-+
-+- Artifact Imported
-+- Artifact Rejected
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Parser
-+
-+- Parsing Started
-+- Parsing Completed
-+- Parsing Failed
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Assets
-+
-+- Asset Extracted
-+- Asset Validation Failed
-+
-+---
-+
-+## References
-+
-+- Reference Discovered
-+- Reference Resolved
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Validation
-+
-+- Validation Started
-+- Validation Passed
-+- Validation Failed
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Queue
-+
-+- Queue Candidate Created
-+- Queue Candidate Approved
-+- Queue Candidate Rejected
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Governance
-+
-+- Review Started
-+- Review Completed
-+- Promotion Approved
-+- Promotion Rejected
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Publication
-+
-+- Publication Started
-+- Publication Completed
-+
-+---
-+
-+## System
-+
-+- Service Started
-+- Service Stopped
-+- Configuration Updated
-+- Recovery Completed
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Consumers
-+
-+Events MAY be consumed by:
-+
-+- Monitoring
-+- Reporting
-+- Analytics
-+- Repository Indexing
-+- Audit Services
-+- Automation
-+
-+Consumers SHALL NOT modify historical events.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Retention
-+
-+Events SHOULD remain available according to repository retention policies.
-+
-+Historical events constitute institutional evidence.
-+
-+Events SHALL remain reconstructable from archival storage.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Every event SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Required metadata
-+- Event type
-+- Timestamp
-+- Identifier format
-+- Version compatibility
-+
-+Invalid events SHALL be rejected.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Artifacts preserve evidence.
-+
-+Events preserve activity.
-+
-+Together they provide a complete institutional history of both what exists and what has occurred.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
