-+# Event Processing Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Event Processing Specification defines how repository components consume, evaluate, and respond to events.
-+
-+Event processing performs work in response to events.
-+
-+Event processing SHALL NOT alter historical event records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Events remain immutable.
-+- Processing is deterministic.
-+- Processing is idempotent.
-+- Processing is observable.
-+- Processing preserves provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Event consumers
-+- Event handlers
-+- Workflow services
-+- Automation services
-+- Analytics services
-+- Repository maintenance services
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Processing Model
-+
-+Every event SHALL progress through the following stages:
-+
-+1. Receive
-+2. Validate
-+3. Classify
-+4. Process
-+5. Record Results
-+6. Complete
-+
-+Each stage SHALL be independently observable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Reception
-+
-+Consumers SHALL:
-+
-+- Accept supported event versions.
-+- Verify event integrity.
-+- Reject malformed events.
-+- Preserve the original event.
-+
-+Reception SHALL generate operational diagnostics.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Prior to processing, consumers SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Event schema validity.
-+- Event type.
-+- Event version.
-+- Required metadata.
-+- Provenance reference.
-+
-+Invalid events SHALL NOT continue processing.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Classification
-+
-+Consumers MAY classify events according to:
-+
-+- Event Category
-+- Event Type
-+- Source Component
-+- Severity
-+- Correlation ID
-+- Lifecycle State
-+
-+Classification SHALL NOT modify the event.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Processing
-+
-+Processing SHALL execute according to approved service contracts.
-+
-+Processing MAY include:
-+
-+- Repository indexing
-+- Metrics collection
-+- Audit recording
-+- Queue updates
-+- Notification generation
-+- Workflow progression
-+
-+Processing SHALL preserve repository integrity.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Idempotency
-+
-+Consumers SHALL safely process duplicate events.
-+
-+Repeated processing of the same event SHALL NOT produce inconsistent repository state.
-+
-+Duplicate detection SHOULD use Event ID.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Processing Results
-+
-+Processing MAY produce:
-+
-+- Repository updates
-+- Derived artifacts
-+- Operational metrics
-+- Additional events
-+- Execution reports
-+
-+Results SHALL reference the originating event.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Error Handling
-+
-+Processing errors SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve the original event.
-+- Record diagnostics.
-+- Identify the failing component.
-+- Support retry where appropriate.
-+
-+Processing failures SHALL generate operational events.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Retry Behavior
-+
-+Recoverable failures MAY be retried.
-+
-+Retries SHOULD:
-+
-+- Preserve Event ID.
-+- Preserve Correlation ID.
-+- Record retry count.
-+- Prevent infinite retry loops.
-+
-+Retry policies SHALL be configurable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Processing Order
-+
-+Where ordering is required:
-+
-+- Events SHALL be processed chronologically.
-+- Correlated events SHOULD preserve workflow order.
-+
-+Where ordering is not required, parallel processing MAY be used.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Execution Reports
-+
-+Each processing operation SHOULD produce a report containing:
-+
-+- Event ID
-+- Consumer
-+- Processing Start
-+- Processing End
-+- Duration
-+- Result
-+- Diagnostics
-+
-+Execution reports support auditing and troubleshooting.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Processing infrastructure SHOULD monitor:
-+
-+- Processing throughput
-+- Success rate
-+- Failure rate
-+- Retry rate
-+- Processing latency
-+- Consumer utilization
-+
-+Operational metrics SHOULD support continuous improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Event processing integrates with:
-+
-+- Event Model
-+- Event Schema
-+- Event Routing
-+- Observability
-+- Validation
-+- Lifecycle
-+- Repository Indexes
-+
-+Integration SHALL preserve repository consistency.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Events record what has happened.
-+
-+Processing determines what should happen next.
-+
-+By separating historical facts from operational behavior, the Repository Ingestion Framework preserves both institutional memory and implementation flexibility.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
