-+# Contents
-+````markdown
-+# Ingestion Glossary
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Ingestion Glossary establishes the canonical vocabulary used throughout the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Specifications SHALL use these definitions consistently.
-+
-+When ambiguity exists, this glossary is authoritative.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Definitions
-+
-+## Artifact
-+
-+A unit of evidence ingested by the repository.
-+
-+Examples include conversations, PDFs, Markdown files, JSON documents, images, and research papers.
-+
-+Artifacts are immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Asset
-+
-+A reusable component extracted from an artifact.
-+
-+Examples include templates, diagrams, code blocks, prompts, checklists, and specifications.
-+
-+Assets retain provenance from their parent artifact.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Canonical Artifact
-+
-+A repository artifact that has successfully completed review and promotion.
-+
-+Canonical artifacts represent governed repository knowledge.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Queue Candidate
-+
-+A provisional observation generated during ingestion.
-+
-+Queue candidates await review.
-+
-+Queue candidates are not decisions.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Queue
-+
-+A managed collection of queue candidates sharing a common purpose.
-+
-+Queues support governance workflows.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Provenance
-+
-+The complete chain of custody describing where repository objects originated and how they evolved.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Lineage
-+
-+The sequence of parent-child relationships connecting derived objects to their originating artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Relationship
-+
-+An explicit connection between two repository objects.
-+
-+Relationships are repository objects.
-+
-+Relationships retain provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Reference
-+
-+A discovered mention of another resource.
-+
-+References are observations.
-+
-+Relationships are interpretations.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Structural Parsing
-+
-+The process of observing and recording the structure of an artifact without interpreting its meaning.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Semantic Extraction
-+
-+The process of deriving concepts, patterns, principles, or knowledge from structured artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Repository Mapping
-+
-+The process of identifying relationships between repository objects.
-+
-+Repository Mapping does not modify repository contents.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Validation
-+
-+The process of verifying compliance with repository specifications.
-+
-+Validation does not assess correctness of ideas.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Promotion
-+
-+The governance process by which reviewed artifacts become canonical repository knowledge.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Publication
-+
-+The process of making canonical artifacts available within the repository.
-+
-+Publication follows promotion.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Lifecycle
-+
-+The recorded progression of an artifact through repository processing.
-+
-+Lifecycle history is immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Observation
-+
-+A recorded fact extracted from evidence without interpretation.
-+
-+Observations precede knowledge.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Knowledge
-+
-+Information that has passed through repository governance and has become canonical.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Governance
-+
-+The collection of policies and review processes that maintain repository integrity.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Service
-+
-+A component responsible for a single repository function.
-+
-+Services are defined by contracts rather than implementations.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Schema
-+
-+A specification defining the structure of a repository object.
-+
-+Schemas govern repository consistency.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Specification
-+
-+A constitutional document defining repository behavior, structure, or policy.
-+
-+Specifications guide implementation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Repository
-+
-+The governed institutional memory maintained by ADE.
-+
-+The repository contains evidence, knowledge, relationships, and history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Shared language creates shared understanding.
-+
-+Consistent terminology enables consistent engineering.
-+
-+The glossary is part of the repository constitution.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
