-@@ -0,0 +1,222 @@
-+# Observability Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Observability Specification defines how the Repository Ingestion Framework measures, records, and exposes its operational behavior.
-+
-+Observability enables operators to understand the internal state of the system through its externally visible outputs.
-+
-+Observability supports diagnosis.
-+
-+It does not replace validation or governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Every significant operation is observable.
-+- Observability is non-invasive.
-+- Measurements are reproducible.
-+- Operational evidence is preserved.
-+- Observability supports continuous improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+Observability applies to:
-+
-+- Services
-+- Parsers
-+- Validation engines
-+- Repository mapping
-+- Queue processing
-+- Publication workflows
-+- Automation
-+- Supporting infrastructure
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Observability Components
-+
-+The framework SHOULD provide:
-+
-+- Logging
-+- Metrics
-+- Event Streams
-+- Health Reporting
-+- Execution Tracing
-+
-+Each component serves a distinct operational purpose.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Logging
-+
-+Logs SHALL record operational events.
-+
-+Typical log entries include:
-+
-+- Service start
-+- Service completion
-+- Validation failures
-+- Processing warnings
-+- Unexpected exceptions
-+
-+Logs SHOULD support troubleshooting.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Metrics
-+
-+Metrics SHOULD measure:
-+
-+- Processing duration
-+- Throughput
-+- Success rate
-+- Failure rate
-+- Queue size
-+- Validation rate
-+- Publication rate
-+
-+Metrics SHALL be collected consistently.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Event Streams
-+
-+Repository events SHOULD describe significant lifecycle activity.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Artifact Imported
-+- Parsing Completed
-+- Validation Passed
-+- Validation Failed
-+- Queue Candidate Created
-+- Artifact Promoted
-+- Artifact Published
-+
-+Events SHALL remain immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Reporting
-+
-+Every major service SHOULD expose operational health.
-+
-+Health reports MAY include:
-+
-+- Current status
-+- Active version
-+- Dependency status
-+- Resource availability
-+- Recent failures
-+
-+Health reporting SHOULD support automated monitoring.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Execution Tracing
-+
-+Long-running workflows SHOULD support execution tracing.
-+
-+Tracing SHOULD identify:
-+
-+- Workflow identifier
-+- Processing stages
-+- Stage duration
-+- Dependencies
-+- Failure locations
-+
-+Tracing SHOULD simplify diagnosis.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Operational Dashboards
-+
-+Operational dashboards MAY summarize:
-+
-+- Active workflows
-+- Queue depth
-+- Validation status
-+- Repository activity
-+- Error trends
-+- Processing performance
-+
-+Dashboards SHALL visualize repository activity without modifying repository data.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Alerting
-+
-+Operational alerts SHOULD notify operators when:
-+
-+- Critical failures occur.
-+- Validation repeatedly fails.
-+- Queue growth exceeds thresholds.
-+- Repository consistency is threatened.
-+- Required services become unavailable.
-+
-+Alerts SHOULD include sufficient diagnostic context.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Retention
-+
-+Operational observations SHOULD define retention policies.
-+
-+Retention SHOULD balance:
-+
-+- Operational usefulness
-+- Storage requirements
-+- Audit needs
-+- Historical analysis
-+
-+Repository governance SHALL determine retention duration.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Privacy
-+
-+Observability SHALL avoid unnecessary exposure of sensitive information.
-+
-+Logs, metrics, and traces SHOULD contain only the information necessary for operational diagnosis.
-+
-+Sensitive information SHOULD be protected according to repository security policies.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Integration
-+
-+Observability components SHOULD integrate with:
-+
-+- Validation
-+- Quality Assurance
-+- Operational Readiness
-+- Security
-+- Repository Analytics
-+
-+Integration improves institutional awareness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+If repository behavior cannot be observed, it cannot be confidently understood.
-+
-+Observability transforms execution into evidence.
-+
-+Evidence enables diagnosis.
-+
-+Diagnosis enables continuous improvement while preserving the integrity of the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
