-+# Parser Behavior Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Parser Behavior Specification defines the expected behavior of all structural parsers within the ingestion framework.
-+
-+This specification governs behavior rather than implementation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Mission
-+
-+The parser transforms source artifacts into structured repository artifacts.
-+
-+The parser observes.
-+
-+The parser does not interpret.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Principles
-+
-+- Preserve evidence.
-+- Preserve chronology.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Preserve structure.
-+- Never modify source material.
-+- Produce deterministic output.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Inputs
-+
-+The parser SHALL accept supported repository artifacts including:
-+
-+- Conversations
-+- Markdown
-+- PDF
-+- DOCX
-+- TXT
-+- JSON
-+- Future supported formats
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Outputs
-+
-+The parser SHALL produce:
-+
-+- Artifact Record
-+- Structural Representation
-+- Asset Collection
-+- Reference Collection
-+- Queue Candidates
-+- Validation Report
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Responsibilities
-+
-+The parser SHALL identify:
-+
-+- Sections
-+- Headings
-+- Lists
-+- Tables
-+- Code blocks
-+- Conversation turns
-+- Attachments
-+- References
-+- Reusable assets
-+
-+The parser SHALL preserve ordering.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Asset Extraction
-+
-+The parser SHALL extract reusable assets including:
-+
-+- Markdown
-+- JSON
-+- YAML
-+- Source Code
-+- Templates
-+- Diagrams
-+- Tables
-+- Checklists
-+- Folder Structures
-+- Prompt Structures
-+
-+Extracted assets SHALL retain provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Reference Capture
-+
-+The parser SHALL capture references to:
-+
-+- Repository artifacts
-+- Files
-+- URLs
-+- Images
-+- Documents
-+- Standards
-+- External resources
-+
-+Reference resolution occurs later.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Candidate Generation
-+
-+The parser SHALL generate candidate entries for applicable queues.
-+
-+Queue candidates SHALL remain provisional.
-+
-+The parser SHALL NOT promote artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Parser Limitations
-+
-+The parser SHALL NOT:
-+
-+- Summarize
-+- Rewrite
-+- Infer intent
-+- Merge concepts
-+- Delete content
-+- Promote knowledge
-+- Modify evidence
-+
-+These responsibilities belong to downstream services.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Error Handling
-+
-+Parser failures SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve source artifacts.
-+- Record errors.
-+- Preserve successful partial observations.
-+- Never discard evidence.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Success Criteria
-+
-+A successful parse SHALL produce:
-+
-+- Complete structural representation.
-+- Complete provenance.
-+- Complete asset extraction.
-+- Queue candidates.
-+- Validation-ready output.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Parsing is observation.
-+
-+Knowledge is produced later.
-+
-+Observation must remain trustworthy.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
