-+# Publication Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Publication Specification defines how canonical artifacts are published into the repository after successful promotion.
-+
-+Publication is the final operational stage of the ingestion pipeline.
-+
-+Publication SHALL preserve repository integrity.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Principles
-+
-+- Publish only canonical artifacts.
-+- Never overwrite without lineage.
-+- Preserve repository consistency.
-+- Maintain deterministic outputs.
-+- Update repository indexes.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Inputs
-+
-+Publication SHALL require:
-+
-+- Canonical Artifact
-+- Promotion Record
-+- Provenance Record
-+- Repository Mapping
-+- Destination Path
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Outputs
-+
-+Publication SHALL produce:
-+
-+- Published Artifact
-+- Publication Record
-+- Updated Repository Index
-+- Updated Cross References
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Responsibilities
-+
-+The Publication Service SHALL:
-+
-+- Write canonical artifacts.
-+- Preserve directory structure.
-+- Maintain artifact identifiers.
-+- Update indexes.
-+- Preserve lineage.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Record
-+
-+Every publication SHALL record:
-+
-+- Publication ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Timestamp
-+- Destination
-+- Published Version
-+- Publisher
-+- Service Version
-+
-+Publication records SHALL be immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Updates
-+
-+Publication MAY update:
-+
-+- Repository Index
-+- Cross Reference Index
-+- Asset Index
-+- Search Index
-+- Knowledge Graph
-+- Change Log
-+
-+Updates SHALL preserve consistency.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Failure Handling
-+
-+If publication fails:
-+
-+- No partial publication SHALL remain.
-+- Source artifacts SHALL remain unchanged.
-+- Errors SHALL be recorded.
-+- Publication MAY be retried.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Rollback
-+
-+Published artifacts MAY be rolled back.
-+
-+Rollback SHALL:
-+
-+- Record the rollback event.
-+- Restore the previous published state.
-+- Preserve all provenance.
-+- Preserve publication history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+Publication is distribution.
-+
-+Promotion is governance.
-+
-+The two SHALL remain independent.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+An artifact becomes canonical through promotion.
-+
-+It becomes available through publication.
-+
-+These are separate responsibilities.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
