-+# Quality Assurance Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Quality Assurance (QA) Specification defines the policies and procedures used to ensure the Repository Ingestion Framework consistently produces reliable, reproducible, and specification-compliant results.
-+
-+Quality Assurance governs the implementation process.
-+
-+Quality Control verifies individual outputs.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Quality is designed into the system.
-+- Verification is evidence-based.
-+- Specifications define quality expectations.
-+- Failures are recorded, not concealed.
-+- Continuous improvement is encouraged.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+Quality Assurance applies to:
-+
-+- Repository specifications
-+- Schemas
-+- Service contracts
-+- Services
-+- Parsers
-+- Validation engines
-+- Repository mappings
-+- Governance workflows
-+- Supporting documentation
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Quality Objectives
-+
-+The framework SHALL strive to achieve:
-+
-+- Structural correctness
-+- Specification compliance
-+- Deterministic execution
-+- Complete provenance
-+- Repository integrity
-+- Consistent behavior
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Quality Activities
-+
-+Quality Assurance includes:
-+
-+- Specification review
-+- Schema review
-+- Code review
-+- Test execution
-+- Validation audits
-+- Documentation review
-+- Release verification
-+
-+Each activity SHALL produce objective evidence.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Review Process
-+
-+Repository artifacts SHOULD undergo review before approval.
-+
-+Reviews SHOULD evaluate:
-+
-+- Correctness
-+- Completeness
-+- Consistency
-+- Clarity
-+- Compliance
-+
-+Review findings SHALL be documented.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Verification
-+
-+Verification SHALL confirm that implementations satisfy their governing specifications.
-+
-+Verification MAY include:
-+
-+- Automated testing
-+- Manual inspection
-+- Contract verification
-+- Schema validation
-+- Performance evaluation
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Validation SHALL determine whether repository outputs satisfy their intended purpose.
-+
-+Validation focuses on usefulness in addition to correctness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Non-Conformities
-+
-+A non-conformity is any deviation from an approved specification.
-+
-+Each non-conformity SHOULD record:
-+
-+- Identifier
-+- Description
-+- Severity
-+- Discovery date
-+- Reporter
-+- Resolution status
-+
-+Non-conformities SHALL remain traceable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Severity Levels
-+
-+The repository SHALL recognize the following severity levels:
-+
-+- Critical
-+- Major
-+- Minor
-+- Informational
-+
-+Severity reflects repository impact.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Corrective Actions
-+
-+Corrective actions SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Root cause analysis
-+- Proposed solution
-+- Verification
-+- Closure documentation
-+
-+Corrective actions SHALL preserve repository history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Preventive Actions
-+
-+Preventive actions SHOULD identify:
-+
-+- Potential risks
-+- Process improvements
-+- Documentation updates
-+- Test additions
-+
-+Preventive actions reduce future defects.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Release Quality
-+
-+Before publication, repository releases SHOULD verify:
-+
-+- All required tests pass.
-+- Critical defects are resolved.
-+- Specifications remain consistent.
-+- Documentation is current.
-+- Repository indexes are synchronized.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Continuous Improvement
-+
-+Quality Assurance SHOULD evolve through:
-+
-+- Retrospectives
-+- Metrics
-+- Lessons learned
-+- Specification refinement
-+- Automation improvements
-+
-+Improvements SHALL preserve repository governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Quality Records
-+
-+The repository SHOULD maintain records for:
-+
-+- Reviews
-+- Test executions
-+- Validation reports
-+- Corrective actions
-+- Preventive actions
-+- Release approvals
-+
-+Quality records constitute repository evidence.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Quality is not inspected into the repository after implementation.
-+
-+Quality emerges from disciplined specifications, careful engineering, objective verification, and transparent governance.
-+
-+The Repository Ingestion Framework treats quality as an institutional responsibility rather than an individual achievement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
