-+# Queue Candidate Schema
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Queue Candidate Schema defines the canonical representation of provisional queue entries generated during ingestion.
-+
-+Queue candidates are observations.
-+
-+They are not decisions.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Queue candidates are immutable.
-+- Queue candidates retain provenance.
-+- Queue candidates are provisional.
-+- Queue candidates support human review.
-+- Queue candidates may be promoted or rejected.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Required Fields
-+
-+Every queue candidate SHALL contain:
-+
-+- Queue Candidate ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Queue Type
-+- Source Location
-+- Candidate Title
-+- Candidate Description
-+- Provenance Record
-+- Timestamp
-+- Parser Version
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Optional Fields
-+
-+A queue candidate MAY contain:
-+
-+- Confidence
-+- Related Artifact IDs
-+- Suggested Destination
-+- Tags
-+- Reviewer Notes
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Candidate States
-+
-+Queue candidates SHALL exist in one of the following states:
-+
-+- New
-+- Under Review
-+- Accepted
-+- Deferred
-+- Rejected
-+- Promoted
-+- Archived
-+
-+State transitions SHALL be recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Types
-+
-+Supported queue types include:
-+
-+- Decision Review
-+- Concept
-+- Observation
-+- Tool
-+- Template
-+- Visualization
-+- Infrastructure
-+- Cross Reference
-+- Open Question
-+- Constitutional
-+- Promotion
-+- Meta Improvement
-+
-+Additional queue types MAY be defined by future specifications.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Provenance
-+
-+Each queue candidate SHALL retain:
-+
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+- Source Section
-+- Source Offset (when available)
-+- Parser Version
-+- Creation Timestamp
-+
-+Queue candidates SHALL never lose provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Review
-+
-+Queue candidates SHALL support:
-+
-+- Acceptance
-+- Rejection
-+- Deferral
-+- Promotion
-+- Commenting
-+
-+Review actions SHALL become part of provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Lifecycle
-+
-+Queue candidates SHALL NOT be deleted.
-+
-+Obsolete candidates SHALL be archived.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Queue candidates represent possibilities.
-+
-+Repository governance determines outcomes.
-+
-+The schema preserves the distinction.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
