-+# Queue Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+Queues provide deterministic staging areas between structural parsing, semantic extraction, and canonical promotion.
-+
-+Queues preserve discoveries while preventing premature interpretation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Contract
-+
-+Every queue shall define:
-+
-+- Purpose
-+- Accepted Inputs
-+- Required Metadata
-+- Review Requirement
-+- Promotion Targets
-+- Retention Policy
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Standard Metadata
-+
-+Every queued item shall include:
-+
-+- Queue ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Source
-+- Provenance
-+- Timestamp
-+- Confidence (if applicable)
-+- Reviewer
-+- Status
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Definitions
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Decision Review Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture explicit decisions made within source artifacts.
-+
-+### Inputs
-+
-+- Conversations
-+- ADRs
-+- Governance documents
-+
-+### Review
-+
-+**Immediate**
-+
-+Explicit decisions should be reviewed immediately following conversation ingestion.
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+- ADR
-+- Governance
-+- Canonical Repository
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Concept Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture candidate concepts requiring evaluation.
-+
-+### Inputs
-+
-+- Conversations
-+- Documentation
-+- Research
-+
-+### Review
-+
-+Scheduled
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+- OBS
-+- Knowledge Base
-+- Canonical Concepts
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Observation Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture observations suitable for structured OBS records.
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+- OBS Repository
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Tool Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture ideas for scripts, utilities, automations, services, or facets.
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+- Utility Specifications
-+- Development Backlog
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Template Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture reusable templates.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Markdown
-+- JSON
-+- YAML
-+- Prompts
-+- Checklists
-+- Specifications
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+Repository Templates
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Visualization Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture reusable visual artifacts.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Mermaid diagrams
-+- Flowcharts
-+- Graphs
-+- Charts
-+- Matrices
-+- Decision trees
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+Visualization Library
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Infrastructure Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture repository architecture changes.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Folder structures
-+- Naming conventions
-+- Repository organization
-+- Build process
-+- Automation
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+Infrastructure Documentation
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Cross-Reference Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Identify potential links between repository artifacts.
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+Repository Index
-+
-+Knowledge Graph
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Open Question Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture unresolved questions.
-+
-+Questions remain open until resolved or intentionally closed.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Constitutional Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture proposed constitutional or governance amendments.
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+Constitution
-+
-+Governance Documents
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Promotion Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Collect reviewed artifacts eligible for canonical publication.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Meta-Improvement Queue
-+
-+### Purpose
-+
-+Capture recommendations for improving the ingestion pipeline itself.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- New queue types
-+- Better schemas
-+- Improved parsing rules
-+- Service refinements
-+- Workflow optimizations
-+
-+### Promotion Targets
-+
-+AIS
-+
-+Queue Specification
-+
-+Service Contracts
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue States
-+
-+Each queue item shall exist in one of the following states:
-+
-+- New
-+- Under Review
-+- Accepted
-+- Deferred
-+- Rejected
-+- Promoted
-+- Archived
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+Queues preserve information.
-+
-+Queues do not interpret information.
-+
-+Queues separate discovery from decision.
-+
-+Human review governs promotion.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
