-+# Contents
-+````markdown
-+# Reference Schema
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Reference Schema defines the canonical representation of references discovered during artifact ingestion.
-+
-+References identify connections to internal and external resources without asserting semantic relationships.
-+
-+Reference resolution is performed by downstream services.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- References are observations.
-+- References retain provenance.
-+- References are immutable.
-+- References do not imply validity.
-+- References do not imply relationship.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Required Fields
-+
-+Every reference SHALL contain:
-+
-+- Reference ID
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+- Reference Type
-+- Reference Value
-+- Source Location
-+- Provenance Record
-+- Discovery Timestamp
-+- Parser Version
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Optional Fields
-+
-+References MAY include:
-+
-+- Display Text
-+- Description
-+- Confidence
-+- Related Artifact ID
-+- Resolution Status
-+- Notes
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Supported Reference Types
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Repository Artifact
-+- File
-+- Directory
-+- URL
-+- DOI
-+- ISBN
-+- Image
-+- Video
-+- Audio
-+- Citation
-+- Email Address
-+- Issue Number
-+- Commit Hash
-+- Branch Name
-+- Tag
-+- Standard
-+- Specification
-+- API Endpoint
-+
-+Additional reference types MAY be introduced through future specifications.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Resolution Status
-+
-+References SHALL exist in one of the following states:
-+
-+- Unresolved
-+- Resolved
-+- Broken
-+- Ambiguous
-+- Archived
-+
-+Resolution SHALL NOT alter the original reference.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Provenance
-+
-+Every reference SHALL retain:
-+
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+- Source Section
-+- Source Offset (when available)
-+- Extraction Method
-+- Parser Version
-+- Timestamp
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+A valid reference SHALL:
-+
-+- Reference an existing parent artifact.
-+- Declare a reference type.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Preserve the original reference value.
-+
-+Reference validity is not required for successful ingestion.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Relationship to Repository Mapping
-+
-+Reference extraction records that a reference exists.
-+
-+Repository Mapping determines what that reference means.
-+
-+These are separate responsibilities.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+A reference is evidence that something was mentioned.
-+
-+Meaning is established later.
-+
-+Observation always precedes interpretation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
