-+# Contents
-+````markdown
-+# Repository Index Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Repository Index Specification defines the canonical indexing system for repository artifacts, assets, relationships, and supporting records.
-+
-+Indexes accelerate discovery.
-+
-+Indexes do not replace repository artifacts.
-+
-+Indexes SHALL always be reproducible from canonical repository data.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Indexes are derived.
-+- Indexes are reproducible.
-+- Indexes preserve references.
-+- Indexes never become the source of truth.
-+- Indexes improve discoverability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Index Categories
-+
-+The repository SHALL support the following logical indexes:
-+
-+- Artifact Index
-+- Asset Index
-+- Relationship Index
-+- Queue Index
-+- Reference Index
-+- Canonical Artifact Index
-+- Lifecycle Index
-+- Provenance Index
-+
-+Additional indexes MAY be introduced by future specifications.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Artifact Index
-+
-+Tracks every artifact known to the repository.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Title
-+- Artifact Type
-+- Lifecycle State
-+- Repository Location
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Asset Index
-+
-+Tracks reusable assets extracted from artifacts.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Asset ID
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+- Asset Type
-+- Repository Location
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Relationship Index
-+
-+Tracks repository relationships.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Relationship ID
-+- Source Artifact ID
-+- Target Artifact ID
-+- Relationship Type
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Index
-+
-+Tracks active queue candidates.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Queue Candidate ID
-+- Queue Type
-+- Current State
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Reference Index
-+
-+Tracks discovered references.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Reference ID
-+- Reference Type
-+- Resolution Status
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Artifact Index
-+
-+Tracks published canonical artifacts.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Canonical ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Version
-+- Publication Date
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Lifecycle Index
-+
-+Tracks lifecycle state for repository artifacts.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Current Lifecycle State
-+- Last Transition Timestamp
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Provenance Index
-+
-+Tracks provenance records.
-+
-+Each entry SHALL include:
-+
-+- Provenance ID
-+- Parent Artifact ID
-+- Latest Transformation Event
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Index Maintenance
-+
-+Indexes SHALL be updated after:
-+
-+- Publication
-+- Promotion
-+- Lifecycle transitions
-+- Relationship creation
-+- Asset extraction
-+- Queue promotion
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Indexes SHALL:
-+
-+- Reference existing objects.
-+- Contain unique identifiers.
-+- Preserve referential integrity.
-+- Be reproducible.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Failure Handling
-+
-+Index failures SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve existing indexes.
-+- Record errors.
-+- Permit reconstruction.
-+
-+Indexes SHALL never corrupt repository artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Artifacts contain knowledge.
-+
-+Indexes enable navigation.
-+
-+Navigation is a service, not the repository itself.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
