-+# Repository Mapping Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+Repository Mapping identifies relationships between newly ingested artifacts and existing repository content.
-+
-+Mapping is observational.
-+
-+Mapping does not modify repository contents.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Objectives
-+
-+- Prevent duplication
-+- Preserve historical lineage
-+- Discover relationships
-+- Suggest consolidation
-+- Maintain repository coherence
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Mapping Inputs
-+
-+- Artifact Record
-+- Structural Assets
-+- Queue Candidates
-+- Repository Index
-+- Canonical Artifacts
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Mapping Outputs
-+
-+Each mapping SHALL produce one or more relationship records.
-+
-+Relationship records SHALL retain provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Relationship Types
-+
-+## Existing Match
-+
-+The artifact already exists.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Duplicate
-+
-+The artifact substantially duplicates an existing artifact.
-+
-+No automatic deletion occurs.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Related
-+
-+The artifact is related to one or more existing artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Extension
-+
-+The artifact expands an existing concept.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Supersedes
-+
-+The artifact replaces an earlier artifact.
-+
-+Superseded artifacts remain preserved.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Superseded By
-+
-+Inverse relationship.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Merge Candidate
-+
-+Multiple artifacts may be consolidated after review.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Reference
-+
-+The artifact references another repository object.
-+
-+---
-+
-+## Standalone
-+
-+No meaningful relationships discovered.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Mapping Criteria
-+
-+Mapping MAY consider:
-+
-+- Artifact IDs
-+- Titles
-+- References
-+- Structural similarity
-+- Asset similarity
-+- Shared provenance
-+- Queue overlap
-+
-+Criteria SHALL be transparent.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Human Review
-+
-+Repository Mapping SHALL NOT:
-+
-+- Delete artifacts
-+- Merge artifacts
-+- Rewrite artifacts
-+- Promote artifacts
-+
-+Those actions require downstream review.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Mapping Record
-+
-+Each mapping SHALL include:
-+
-+- Mapping ID
-+- Artifact ID
-+- Relationship Type
-+- Related Artifact ID
-+- Confidence
-+- Timestamp
-+- Service Version
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+Discovery before action.
-+
-+Relationships before restructuring.
-+
-+Repository integrity over convenience.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
