-+# Repository Relationship Schema
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1
-+**Status:** Draft
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Repository Relationship Schema defines the canonical representation of relationships between repository artifacts.
-+
-+Relationships are first-class repository objects.
-+
-+They describe how artifacts relate without modifying the artifacts themselves.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Relationships are explicit.
-+- Relationships are directional.
-+- Relationships retain provenance.
-+- Relationships are immutable once recorded.
-+- Relationships may evolve through superseding records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Required Fields
-+
-+Every relationship SHALL contain:
-+
-+- Relationship ID
-+- Source Artifact ID
-+- Target Artifact ID
-+- Relationship Type
-+- Provenance Record
-+- Creation Timestamp
-+- Service Version
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Optional Fields
-+
-+Relationships MAY include:
-+
-+- Confidence
-+- Reviewer
-+- Notes
-+- Supporting Evidence
-+- Related Queue Candidate IDs
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Relationship Types
-+
-+Supported relationship types include:
-+
-+- References
-+- Referenced By
-+- Related To
-+- Derived From
-+- Parent Of
-+- Child Of
-+- Depends On
-+- Dependency Of
-+- Extends
-+- Extended By
-+- Supersedes
-+- Superseded By
-+- Duplicate Of
-+- Duplicate Source
-+- Implements
-+- Implemented By
-+- Replaces
-+- Replaced By
-+
-+Additional relationship types MAY be introduced through future specifications.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Relationship Direction
-+
-+Every relationship SHALL have a defined direction.
-+
-+Example:
-+
-+Artifact A
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Derived From
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Artifact B
-+
-+The inverse relationship SHALL be derivable or explicitly recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Provenance
-+
-+Relationships SHALL preserve:
-+
-+- Originating Artifact
-+- Mapping Service
-+- Creation Timestamp
-+- Supporting Evidence
-+- Repository Version
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Lifecycle
-+
-+Relationships SHALL exist in one of the following states:
-+
-+- Active
-+- Superseded
-+- Archived
-+
-+Relationships SHALL NOT be deleted.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+A valid relationship SHALL:
-+
-+- Reference existing Artifact IDs
-+- Use a recognized Relationship Type
-+- Retain provenance
-+- Preserve directionality
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Knowledge grows through relationships.
-+
-+Artifacts contain evidence.
-+
-+Relationships create context.
-+
-+Context enables understanding.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
