-+# Security and Integrity Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Security and Integrity Specification defines the principles and requirements that protect repository evidence, preserve institutional knowledge, and maintain trust in the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Security protects repository assets.
-+
-+Integrity protects repository truth.
-+
-+Both are essential.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Preserve evidence.
-+- Protect provenance.
-+- Record accountability.
-+- Minimize trust assumptions.
-+- Detect unauthorized changes.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Repository artifacts
-+- Assets
-+- Schemas
-+- Specifications
-+- Service contracts
-+- Services
-+- Parsers
-+- Repository indexes
-+- Governance records
-+- Operational metadata
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integrity
-+
-+Repository integrity SHALL ensure:
-+
-+- Artifacts remain unaltered.
-+- Provenance remains complete.
-+- Relationships remain valid.
-+- Identifiers remain unique.
-+- History remains preserved.
-+
-+Integrity violations SHALL be recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Evidence Protection
-+
-+Original artifacts SHALL:
-+
-+- Remain immutable.
-+- Preserve original metadata where available.
-+- Retain provenance.
-+- Never be silently replaced.
-+
-+Derived artifacts SHALL reference their source artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Access Control
-+
-+Repository operations SHOULD distinguish between:
-+
-+- Read access
-+- Write access
-+- Review authority
-+- Promotion authority
-+- Administrative authority
-+
-+Authority SHOULD be granted according to governance responsibilities.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Authentication
-+
-+Operational implementations SHOULD authenticate:
-+
-+- Users
-+- Services
-+- Automated processes
-+
-+Authentication mechanisms SHALL be documented.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Authorization
-+
-+Authorized actions SHOULD be governed by repository roles.
-+
-+No implementation SHOULD assume unrestricted modification privileges.
-+
-+Authorization decisions SHOULD be auditable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Trail
-+
-+The repository SHALL record:
-+
-+- Significant operations
-+- Lifecycle transitions
-+- Promotion decisions
-+- Publication events
-+- Administrative changes
-+
-+Audit records SHALL be immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Change Detection
-+
-+The repository SHOULD detect:
-+
-+- Unauthorized modifications
-+- Missing artifacts
-+- Broken relationships
-+- Identifier conflicts
-+- Index inconsistencies
-+
-+Detected issues SHALL generate repository events.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Data Integrity
-+
-+Repository data SHOULD be periodically verified for:
-+
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Referential integrity
-+- Provenance completeness
-+- Index consistency
-+- Lifecycle consistency
-+
-+Integrity verification SHOULD be repeatable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Backup and Recovery
-+
-+Operational deployments SHOULD support:
-+
-+- Repository backup
-+- Metadata backup
-+- Index reconstruction
-+- Provenance preservation
-+- Recovery verification
-+
-+Recovery SHALL preserve institutional history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Incident Management
-+
-+Security or integrity incidents SHOULD record:
-+
-+- Incident identifier
-+- Discovery time
-+- Affected components
-+- Severity
-+- Corrective actions
-+- Resolution status
-+
-+Incidents become part of repository history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Security Reviews
-+
-+Periodic reviews SHOULD evaluate:
-+
-+- Access controls
-+- Audit completeness
-+- Dependency risks
-+- Configuration integrity
-+- Repository integrity metrics
-+
-+Review outcomes SHOULD inform future improvements.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Security protects the repository from unauthorized change.
-+
-+Integrity protects the repository from unintended change.
-+
-+Together they preserve confidence that institutional knowledge remains authentic, traceable, and trustworthy across the lifetime of the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
