-+# Service Contracts
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+Service Contracts define the responsibilities, inputs, outputs, guarantees, and limitations of each service within the ingestion framework.
-+
-+Implementations may vary, but service contracts SHALL remain stable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# General Service Contract
-+
-+Every service SHALL define:
-+
-+- Purpose
-+- Inputs
-+- Outputs
-+- Responsibilities
-+- Guarantees
-+- Limitations
-+- Failure Conditions
-+- Success Criteria
-+
-+Services SHALL be independently testable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Artifact Intake Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Accept repository artifacts and create immutable ingestion records.
-+
-+### Inputs
-+
-+- Conversation
-+- PDF
-+- DOCX
-+- Markdown
-+- TXT
-+- JSON
-+- Repository documents
-+- Future artifact types
-+
-+### Outputs
-+
-+- Artifact Record
-+- Metadata
-+- Provenance Record
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+- Original preserved
-+- Unique Artifact ID assigned
-+- Provenance initialized
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Structural Parsing Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Extract observable structure without interpretation.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Capture:
-+
-+- Sections
-+- Chronology
-+- Conversation turns
-+- Headings
-+- Lists
-+- Tables
-+- Code blocks
-+- Diagrams
-+- Templates
-+- References
-+- Assets
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+No semantic interpretation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Queue Generation Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Generate candidate queue entries from structural observations.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Populate candidate entries for:
-+
-+- Decision Review
-+- Concept
-+- Observation
-+- Tool
-+- Template
-+- Visualization
-+- Infrastructure
-+- Cross-Reference
-+- Open Question
-+- Constitutional
-+- Promotion
-+- Meta-Improvement
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+Queue assignments remain provisional.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Semantic Extraction Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Derive higher-level meaning from structured artifacts.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Identify:
-+
-+- Concepts
-+- Principles
-+- Patterns
-+- Decisions
-+- Governance
-+- Relationships
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+Every semantic object retains provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Mapping Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Determine relationships between ingested artifacts and existing repository content.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Identify:
-+
-+- Existing artifacts
-+- Duplicates
-+- Superseded artifacts
-+- Merge candidates
-+- Cross references
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+No automatic overwrite.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Promotion Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Promote reviewed artifacts into canonical repository locations.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Create canonical repository objects.
-+
-+Maintain lineage.
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+Promotion requires review.
-+
-+History is preserved.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Verify artifact integrity and specification compliance.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+Validate:
-+
-+- Metadata
-+- Provenance
-+- Structural completeness
-+- Queue candidates
-+- Schema compliance
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+Validation is deterministic.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Publication Service
-+
-+## Purpose
-+
-+Publish approved canonical artifacts to repository destinations.
-+
-+### Responsibilities
-+
-+- Write repository files
-+- Preserve history
-+- Update indexes
-+- Maintain references
-+
-+### Guarantees
-+
-+Publication does not alter source artifacts.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Common Invariants
-+
-+Every service SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve provenance
-+- Preserve Artifact IDs
-+- Preserve lineage
-+- Produce deterministic outputs
-+- Avoid silent data loss
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Error Handling
-+
-+Failures SHALL:
-+
-+- Report explicit errors
-+- Preserve partial work
-+- Never corrupt source artifacts
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Services define behavior.
-+
-+Implementations fulfill behavior.
-+
-+Architecture depends on contracts, not technologies.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
