-+# Testing Strategy Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Testing Strategy Specification defines the principles, scope, and structure of testing for the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Testing demonstrates that implementations conform to repository specifications.
-+
-+Testing provides evidence of correctness rather than assumptions of correctness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Every implementation SHALL be testable.
-+- Tests SHALL be deterministic.
-+- Tests SHALL preserve reproducibility.
-+- Automated testing is preferred.
-+- Tests SHALL verify behavior against specifications.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Testing Objectives
-+
-+Testing SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Functional correctness
-+- Specification compliance
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Service contract compliance
-+- Repository integrity
-+- Deterministic behavior
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Test Categories
-+
-+The Repository Ingestion Framework SHALL support:
-+
-+- Unit Tests
-+- Integration Tests
-+- Contract Tests
-+- Schema Validation Tests
-+- Regression Tests
-+- Performance Tests
-+- End-to-End Tests
-+
-+Additional categories MAY be introduced through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Unit Testing
-+
-+Unit tests verify individual components.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Parser methods
-+- Validation functions
-+- Identifier generation
-+- Utility functions
-+
-+Unit tests SHOULD execute independently.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Integration Testing
-+
-+Integration tests verify interactions between services.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+- Intake to parser
-+- Parser to extraction
-+- Extraction to validation
-+- Validation to repository mapping
-+
-+Integration tests SHALL verify interface compatibility.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Contract Testing
-+
-+Contract tests verify compliance with approved service contracts.
-+
-+Each public service interface SHOULD have corresponding contract tests.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Schema Validation Testing
-+
-+Schema tests SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Required fields
-+- Optional fields
-+- Identifier formats
-+- Version compatibility
-+- Referential integrity
-+
-+Schema validation SHALL precede publication.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Regression Testing
-+
-+Regression tests SHALL verify that existing functionality remains unchanged after modifications.
-+
-+Previously resolved defects SHOULD receive regression coverage.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Performance Testing
-+
-+Performance testing SHOULD evaluate:
-+
-+- Processing time
-+- Memory consumption
-+- Throughput
-+- Scalability
-+
-+Performance optimization SHALL NOT compromise correctness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# End-to-End Testing
-+
-+End-to-end tests verify complete repository workflows.
-+
-+Typical workflow:
-+
-+1. Import artifact.
-+2. Parse artifact.
-+3. Extract assets.
-+4. Validate outputs.
-+5. Map relationships.
-+6. Promote canonical knowledge.
-+7. Publish results.
-+
-+The workflow SHALL complete successfully.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Test Data
-+
-+Test artifacts SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Minimal examples
-+- Typical examples
-+- Large artifacts
-+- Invalid artifacts
-+- Corrupted artifacts
-+- Edge cases
-+
-+Test data SHALL remain under version control.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Test Reports
-+
-+Each test execution SHOULD record:
-+
-+- Test identifier
-+- Component tested
-+- Specification version
-+- Result
-+- Duration
-+- Failures
-+- Warnings
-+
-+Reports SHOULD support auditing and troubleshooting.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Continuous Testing
-+
-+Automated testing SHOULD occur:
-+
-+- Before merges
-+- Before releases
-+- After specification updates
-+- After dependency updates
-+
-+Critical failures SHOULD prevent release.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Success Criteria
-+
-+A component SHALL be considered verified when:
-+
-+- Required tests pass.
-+- Contract compliance is demonstrated.
-+- Schema validation succeeds.
-+- No unresolved critical defects remain.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Testing provides objective evidence that implementations satisfy the repository constitution.
-+
-+Specifications define expected behavior.
-+
-+Tests demonstrate that the behavior has been achieved.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
