-+++ /storage/emulated/0/FILE_LIBRARY_UPLOADS/99_UTILITIES/Ingestion/Workflow_Governance_Specification_v0.1.md	2026-07-28 02:52:37.354665554 -0500
-@@ -0,0 +1,306 @@
-+# Workflow Governance Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Governance Specification defines the policies, responsibilities, approval processes, and controls governing the creation, modification, deployment, execution, and retirement of workflow definitions.
-+
-+Governance ensures that workflows evolve in a controlled, auditable, and institutionally consistent manner.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Governance is policy-driven.
-+- Workflow ownership is explicit.
-+- Changes are traceable.
-+- Decisions are auditable.
-+- Governance preserves institutional knowledge.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Definitions
-+- Workflow Versions
-+- Workflow Execution Policies
-+- Workflow Publication
-+- Workflow Retirement
-+- Workflow Review
-+- Workflow Change Management
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Objectives
-+
-+Workflow governance SHALL ensure:
-+
-+- Consistent workflow quality.
-+- Controlled evolution.
-+- Repository integrity.
-+- Regulatory compliance where applicable.
-+- Long-term maintainability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Roles
-+
-+Workflow governance SHALL recognize the following roles.
-+
-+| Role | Responsibility |
-+|------|----------------|
-+| Workflow Author | Creates workflow definitions |
-+| Workflow Reviewer | Performs technical review |
-+| Workflow Approver | Authorizes publication |
-+| Workflow Owner | Maintains workflow lifecycle |
-+| Repository Administrator | Manages repository operations |
-+| Governance Authority | Defines workflow governance policy |
-+
-+Organizations MAY define additional governance roles.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Workflow Ownership
-+
-+Every workflow SHALL have a designated owner.
-+
-+Workflow ownership SHALL include responsibility for:
-+
-+- Maintenance
-+- Documentation
-+- Version management
-+- Issue resolution
-+- Retirement planning
-+
-+Ownership SHALL remain current throughout the workflow lifecycle.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Lifecycle
-+
-+Workflow governance SHALL follow the lifecycle:
-+
-+Draft
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Technical Review
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Governance Review
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Approval
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Publication
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Operational Monitoring
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Revision or Deprecation
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Archival
-+
-+Each transition SHALL be recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Workflow Approval
-+
-+Workflow approval SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Technical correctness
-+- Policy compliance
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Documentation completeness
-+- Validation success
-+- Repository compatibility
-+
-+Approval SHALL precede publication.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Change Management
-+
-+Workflow changes SHALL be managed through formal change requests.
-+
-+Each request SHALL include:
-+
-+- Change identifier
-+- Description
-+- Rationale
-+- Expected impact
-+- Risk assessment
-+- Compatibility assessment
-+
-+Change requests SHALL remain permanently associated with the workflow history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Impact Assessment
-+
-+Prior to approval, workflow changes SHALL assess potential impacts on:
-+
-+- Existing executions
-+- Workflow compatibility
-+- Repository schemas
-+- Services
-+- Events
-+- Validation rules
-+- Governance policies
-+
-+Impact assessments SHALL be documented.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Compliance
-+
-+Governed workflows SHALL comply with:
-+
-+- Repository Constitution
-+- Repository Standards
-+- Schema Governance
-+- Security policies
-+- Validation requirements
-+- Versioning policies
-+
-+Non-compliant workflows SHALL NOT become Active.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Exception Management
-+
-+Governance MAY approve temporary exceptions.
-+
-+Every exception SHALL record:
-+
-+- Exception identifier
-+- Scope
-+- Justification
-+- Approval authority
-+- Expiration date
-+- Mitigation strategy
-+
-+Expired exceptions SHALL be reviewed or removed.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Requirements
-+
-+Governance SHALL maintain immutable records of:
-+
-+- Workflow creation
-+- Reviews
-+- Approvals
-+- Publications
-+- Modifications
-+- Deprecations
-+- Retirements
-+
-+Audit records SHALL preserve complete provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Deprecation
-+
-+Workflow deprecation SHALL include:
-+
-+- Deprecation reason
-+- Effective date
-+- Replacement workflow, if applicable
-+- Migration guidance
-+- Owner approval
-+
-+Deprecated workflows SHALL remain historically available.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Retirement
-+
-+Workflow retirement SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve historical executions.
-+- Preserve workflow definitions.
-+- Archive governance records.
-+- Maintain provenance.
-+
-+Retired workflows SHALL NOT be permanently deleted.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Metrics
-+
-+Governance services SHOULD report:
-+
-+- Active workflows
-+- Pending reviews
-+- Approval duration
-+- Change frequency
-+- Deprecation rate
-+- Policy exceptions
-+- Governance compliance rate
-+
-+Metrics SHALL support continuous governance improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Workflow governance SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Ownership
-+- Required approvals
-+- Documentation completeness
-+- Policy compliance
-+- Version compatibility
-+- Repository consistency
-+
-+Validation SHALL occur before publication.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Governance integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Versioning
-+- Workflow Definition Schema
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Schema Governance
-+- Repository Constitution
-+- Repository Standards
-+- Lifecycle Management
-+- Repository Indexes
-+- Observability
-+
-+Governance SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Workflows represent executable institutional knowledge.
-+
-+Governance ensures that this knowledge evolves deliberately, transparently, and responsibly through structured review, accountable ownership, and permanent auditability.
-+
-+By embedding governance into the workflow lifecycle, the Repository Ingestion Framework transforms workflow management from an operational activity into a durable institutional capability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
