-+# Workflow Metrics Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Metrics Specification defines the canonical framework for collecting, calculating, storing, and reporting workflow performance and operational metrics across the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Metrics provide quantitative evidence supporting operational excellence, governance, capacity planning, and continuous improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Metrics are objective.
-+- Metrics are reproducible.
-+- Metrics preserve provenance.
-+- Metrics are implementation-independent.
-+- Metrics support institutional learning.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Definitions
-+- Workflow Executions
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Workflow Recovery
-+- Workflow Replay
-+- Workflow Governance
-+- Operational Monitoring
-+
-+All workflow executions SHALL contribute to the repository's metrics.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Metric Definition
-+
-+A metric is a measurable value derived from one or more workflow events, execution records, or governance activities.
-+
-+Metrics SHALL be calculated from authoritative repository records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Metric Categories
-+
-+Workflow metrics SHALL be organized into the following categories:
-+
-+- Execution Metrics
-+- Performance Metrics
-+- Reliability Metrics
-+- Recovery Metrics
-+- Governance Metrics
-+- Resource Metrics
-+- Quality Metrics
-+- Operational Metrics
-+
-+Additional categories MAY be defined through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Metric Schema
-+
-+Every metric SHALL contain:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Metric ID | Yes | Unique metric identifier |
-+| Metric Name | Yes | Human-readable metric name |
-+| Category | Yes | Metric classification |
-+| Calculation Method | Yes | Defined calculation formula |
-+| Unit | Yes | Measurement unit |
-+| Collection Interval | Yes | Metric aggregation period |
-+| Data Sources | Yes | Repository records used |
-+| Timestamp | Yes | Metric generation time |
-+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Execution Metrics
-+
-+Execution metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Total executions
-+- Successful executions
-+- Failed executions
-+- Cancelled executions
-+- Suspended executions
-+- Active executions
-+
-+Execution metrics SHALL support operational visibility.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Performance Metrics
-+
-+Performance metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Average execution duration
-+- Median execution duration
-+- Step execution duration
-+- Queue wait time
-+- End-to-end processing time
-+- Throughput
-+
-+Performance metrics SHALL identify optimization opportunities.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Reliability Metrics
-+
-+Reliability metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Success rate
-+- Failure rate
-+- Retry frequency
-+- Timeout frequency
-+- Service availability
-+- Dependency failures
-+
-+Reliability metrics SHALL support operational resilience.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Recovery Metrics
-+
-+Recovery metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Recovery attempts
-+- Successful recoveries
-+- Failed recoveries
-+- Average recovery duration
-+- Recovery replay count
-+- Recovery success percentage
-+
-+Recovery metrics SHALL evaluate recovery effectiveness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Metrics
-+
-+Governance metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Workflow approval time
-+- Review duration
-+- Change request volume
-+- Active workflow versions
-+- Deprecated workflows
-+- Governance exceptions
-+
-+Governance metrics SHALL support process improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Resource Metrics
-+
-+Resource metrics MAY include:
-+
-+- CPU utilization
-+- Memory utilization
-+- Storage consumption
-+- Queue depth
-+- Service concurrency
-+- Execution capacity
-+
-+Resource metrics SHALL assist operational planning.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Quality Metrics
-+
-+Quality metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Validation success rate
-+- Validation failures
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Execution consistency
-+- Replay consistency
-+- Audit completeness
-+
-+Quality metrics SHALL support repository integrity.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Operational Metrics
-+
-+Operational metrics SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Event volume
-+- Workflow backlog
-+- Processing latency
-+- Alert frequency
-+- Service health
-+- Repository availability
-+
-+Operational metrics SHALL support monitoring and incident response.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Metric Collection
-+
-+Metric collection SHALL:
-+
-+- Operate continuously.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Avoid altering workflow execution.
-+- Record collection failures.
-+- Support configurable aggregation intervals.
-+
-+Collection SHALL minimize operational overhead.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Metric Validation
-+
-+Metrics SHALL be validated for:
-+
-+- Data completeness
-+- Calculation correctness
-+- Timestamp accuracy
-+- Provenance continuity
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Repository consistency
-+
-+Invalid metrics SHALL NOT be published.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Historical Metrics
-+
-+Historical metrics SHALL:
-+
-+- Remain immutable.
-+- Support trend analysis.
-+- Preserve calculation methodology.
-+- Record schema versions.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+
-+Historical recalculation SHALL generate new metric records rather than overwrite existing records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Reporting
-+
-+Metric reporting SHOULD support:
-+
-+- Dashboards
-+- Operational summaries
-+- Governance reports
-+- Trend analysis
-+- Capacity planning
-+- Audit support
-+
-+Reports SHALL reference the underlying metric records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Metric services SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Collection status
-+- Collection latency
-+- Aggregation duration
-+- Validation failures
-+- Storage utilization
-+- Reporting availability
-+
-+Monitoring SHALL ensure reliable metric generation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Metrics integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Workflow Audit
-+- Workflow Governance
-+- Workflow Recovery
-+- Event Processing
-+- Observability
-+- Repository Indexes
-+- Provenance
-+
-+Metric generation SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Workflows generate evidence through execution.
-+
-+Metrics transform that evidence into measurable institutional knowledge.
-+
-+By grounding every metric in authoritative repository records, the Repository Ingestion Framework enables objective evaluation, informed governance, and continuous improvement while preserving complete transparency and reproducibility.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
