-+# Workflow Reporting Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Reporting Specification defines the canonical framework for producing structured reports describing workflow execution, governance, operational performance, compliance, and historical activity.
-+
-+Reports transform repository records into human-readable institutional knowledge while preserving provenance and reproducibility.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Reports are evidence-based.
-+- Reports are reproducible.
-+- Reports preserve provenance.
-+- Reports are implementation-independent.
-+- Reports are generated from authoritative repository records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Execution Reports
-+- Governance Reports
-+- Operational Reports
-+- Audit Reports
-+- Compliance Reports
-+- Performance Reports
-+- Repository Health Reports
-+
-+All reports SHALL be generated from canonical repository data.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Definition
-+
-+A report is a structured representation of repository information generated for operational, governance, analytical, or compliance purposes.
-+
-+Reports SHALL summarize information without modifying repository records.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Objectives
-+
-+Workflow reporting SHALL provide:
-+
-+- Operational visibility
-+- Governance transparency
-+- Compliance evidence
-+- Performance analysis
-+- Historical insight
-+- Decision support
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Categories
-+
-+Supported report categories include:
-+
-+- Execution Reports
-+- Summary Reports
-+- Exception Reports
-+- Audit Reports
-+- Governance Reports
-+- Performance Reports
-+- Capacity Reports
-+- Compliance Reports
-+- Repository Health Reports
-+
-+Additional report categories MAY be introduced through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Report Schema
-+
-+Every report SHALL contain:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Report ID | Yes | Unique report identifier |
-+| Report Name | Yes | Human-readable report title |
-+| Report Type | Yes | Report classification |
-+| Report Version | Yes | Report schema version |
-+| Generation Timestamp | Yes | Report creation time |
-+| Reporting Period | Yes | Covered time interval |
-+| Data Sources | Yes | Repository records referenced |
-+| Generated By | Yes | Responsible service |
-+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental report information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Execution Reports
-+
-+Execution reports SHOULD summarize:
-+
-+- Workflow executions
-+- Execution duration
-+- Step completion
-+- Success and failure counts
-+- Validation outcomes
-+- Recovery activity
-+
-+Execution reports SHALL support operational diagnostics.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Governance Reports
-+
-+Governance reports SHOULD summarize:
-+
-+- Workflow approvals
-+- Reviews
-+- Change requests
-+- Active versions
-+- Deprecated workflows
-+- Governance exceptions
-+
-+Governance reports SHALL support institutional oversight.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Reports
-+
-+Audit reports SHOULD summarize:
-+
-+- Audit events
-+- Administrative actions
-+- State transitions
-+- Provenance verification
-+- Compliance evidence
-+
-+Audit reports SHALL support traceability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Performance Reports
-+
-+Performance reports SHOULD include:
-+
-+- Average execution duration
-+- Throughput
-+- Queue performance
-+- Resource utilization
-+- Service latency
-+- Bottleneck analysis
-+
-+Performance reports SHALL support optimization.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Compliance Reports
-+
-+Compliance reports SHOULD summarize:
-+
-+- Policy adherence
-+- Validation compliance
-+- Governance compliance
-+- Security controls
-+- Audit completeness
-+- Exception history
-+
-+Compliance reports SHALL support regulatory and organizational requirements.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Health Reports
-+
-+Repository health reports SHOULD summarize:
-+
-+- Service availability
-+- Workflow success rate
-+- Event processing health
-+- Index consistency
-+- Validation health
-+- Storage utilization
-+
-+Health reports SHALL support operational readiness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Generation
-+
-+Report generation SHALL:
-+
-+- Use authoritative repository records.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Record generation events.
-+- Validate report completeness.
-+- Avoid modifying source records.
-+
-+Report generation SHALL be repeatable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Validation
-+
-+Generated reports SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Data completeness
-+- Provenance continuity
-+- Source availability
-+- Reporting period consistency
-+- Calculation correctness
-+
-+Invalid reports SHALL NOT be published.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Historical Reports
-+
-+Historical reports SHALL:
-+
-+- Remain immutable.
-+- Preserve generation metadata.
-+- Reference original repository records.
-+- Support historical comparison.
-+
-+Historical reports SHALL NOT be overwritten.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Retention
-+
-+Reports SHALL follow repository retention policies.
-+
-+Retention SHALL preserve:
-+
-+- Governance evidence
-+- Operational history
-+- Audit documentation
-+- Compliance documentation
-+
-+Archived reports SHALL remain searchable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Report Distribution
-+
-+Reports MAY be distributed through:
-+
-+- Repository dashboards
-+- Administrative interfaces
-+- Scheduled publication
-+- Export services
-+- Notification services
-+- API endpoints
-+
-+Distribution SHALL respect repository security policies.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Reporting services SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Reports generated
-+- Generation duration
-+- Failed report generations
-+- Validation failures
-+- Report storage utilization
-+- Distribution status
-+
-+Monitoring SHALL ensure reporting reliability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Reporting integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Metrics
-+- Workflow Audit
-+- Workflow Governance
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Event Processing
-+- Observability
-+- Repository Indexes
-+- Provenance
-+
-+Reporting SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Repository operations produce authoritative records.
-+
-+Reports organize those records into meaningful institutional narratives without altering the underlying evidence.
-+
-+By separating operational data from its presentation, the Repository Ingestion Framework ensures that reporting remains transparent, reproducible, and grounded in immutable repository history.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
