-+# Workflow Service Capability Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Service Capability Specification defines the canonical model for describing, advertising, validating, and governing the functional capabilities of services participating in the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Capabilities provide the semantic contract that allows workflow orchestration to select appropriate services independently of implementation details.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Capabilities are explicit.
-+- Capabilities are versioned.
-+- Capabilities are independently discoverable.
-+- Capabilities are deterministic.
-+- Capabilities preserve provenance.
-+- Capability definitions are implementation-neutral.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Services
-+- Service Registry
-+- Service Discovery
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Governance Services
-+- Administrative Services
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Definition
-+
-+A capability is a formal declaration describing a unit of functionality that a service provides.
-+
-+Capabilities SHALL describe **what** a service can perform rather than **how** it performs the operation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Objectives
-+
-+Capability definitions SHALL enable:
-+
-+- Service discovery
-+- Workflow planning
-+- Capability validation
-+- Compatibility verification
-+- Governance
-+- Future extensibility
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Capability Schema
-+
-+Every capability definition SHALL contain:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Capability ID | Yes | Unique capability identifier |
-+| Capability Name | Yes | Human-readable capability name |
-+| Capability Version | Yes | Semantic version |
-+| Description | Yes | Functional description |
-+| Capability Category | Yes | Functional classification |
-+| Input Schemas | Yes | Accepted schemas |
-+| Output Schemas | Yes | Produced schemas |
-+| Required Contracts | Yes | Required service contracts |
-+| Supported Workflow Types | Yes | Compatible workflow categories |
-+| Preconditions | No | Required execution conditions |
-+| Postconditions | No | Expected execution results |
-+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental capability information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Identifier
-+
-+Capability identifiers SHALL:
-+
-+- Be globally unique.
-+- Never be reused.
-+- Remain immutable.
-+- Support repository indexing.
-+
-+Example:
-+
-+CAP-PARSE-DOCUMENT
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Categories
-+
-+Capability categories MAY include:
-+
-+- Intake
-+- Parsing
-+- Asset Extraction
-+- Metadata Extraction
-+- Reference Resolution
-+- Validation
-+- Mapping
-+- Transformation
-+- Publication
-+- Governance
-+- Monitoring
-+- Reporting
-+- Utility
-+
-+Additional categories MAY be established through governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Declaration
-+
-+Every registered capability SHALL declare:
-+
-+- Functional purpose
-+- Required inputs
-+- Produced outputs
-+- Execution guarantees
-+- Validation requirements
-+- Related specifications
-+
-+Declarations SHALL remain versioned.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Composition
-+
-+Multiple capabilities MAY be combined to construct larger workflow operations.
-+
-+Composed capabilities SHALL:
-+
-+- Preserve deterministic execution.
-+- Maintain explicit boundaries.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Remain independently testable.
-+
-+Composition SHALL NOT obscure individual capability definitions.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Compatibility
-+
-+Capability compatibility SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Service Contract compatibility
-+- Workflow compatibility
-+- Schema compatibility
-+- Event compatibility
-+- Repository compatibility
-+- API compatibility
-+
-+Compatibility SHALL be explicitly documented.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Discovery
-+
-+Capability discovery SHALL support searching by:
-+
-+- Capability ID
-+- Capability Name
-+- Category
-+- Workflow Type
-+- Supported Contract
-+- Schema Version
-+- Service Provider
-+
-+Discovery SHALL rely upon the authoritative Service Registry.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Validation
-+
-+Capability definitions SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Identifier uniqueness
-+- Schema compliance
-+- Contract compatibility
-+- Workflow compatibility
-+- Version consistency
-+- Governance approval
-+
-+Invalid capabilities SHALL NOT become Active.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Evolution
-+
-+Capabilities MAY evolve through Semantic Versioning.
-+
-+Major versions SHALL indicate incompatible functional changes.
-+
-+Minor versions SHALL introduce backward-compatible enhancements.
-+
-+Patch versions SHALL provide non-breaking refinements.
-+
-+Historical capability definitions SHALL remain preserved.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Lifecycle
-+
-+Capability definitions SHALL progress through:
-+
-+Draft
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Review
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Approved
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Registered
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Active
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Deprecated
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Archived
-+
-+Lifecycle transitions SHALL be governed by repository policy.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Capability Metrics
-+
-+Capability services SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Usage frequency
-+- Successful executions
-+- Failed executions
-+- Average execution duration
-+- Dependent workflows
-+- Registered providers
-+
-+Metrics SHALL support governance and optimization.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Requirements
-+
-+Capability operations SHALL record:
-+
-+- Capability registration
-+- Capability modification
-+- Version publication
-+- Validation results
-+- Discovery operations
-+- Deprecation
-+- Archival
-+
-+Audit records SHALL preserve provenance and remain immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Service Capabilities integrate with:
-+
-+- Workflow Service Registry
-+- Workflow Service Discovery
-+- Workflow Service Contracts
-+- Workflow Definition Schema
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Event Processing
-+- Repository Indexes
-+- Observability
-+
-+Capability management SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Services represent implementations.
-+
-+Capabilities represent institutional functionality.
-+
-+By governing capabilities as first-class repository assets, the Repository Ingestion Framework separates functional intent from implementation, enabling services to evolve independently while preserving deterministic workflow composition, discoverability, interoperability, and long-term architectural stability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
