-+# Workflow Service Discovery Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Service Discovery Specification defines the canonical mechanisms for locating, selecting, validating, and utilizing registered workflow services within the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Service Discovery enables orchestration components to dynamically identify compatible services while preserving deterministic execution and governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Discovery is deterministic.
-+- Discovery is registry-driven.
-+- Discovery is version-aware.
-+- Discovery preserves provenance.
-+- Discovery is independently auditable.
-+- Discovery is implementation-independent.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Service Registry
-+- Parser Services
-+- Validation Services
-+- Mapping Services
-+- Publication Services
-+- Governance Services
-+- Administrative Services
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Definition
-+
-+Service Discovery is the controlled process of identifying services that satisfy the operational requirements of a workflow.
-+
-+Discovery SHALL rely exclusively upon approved Service Registry entries.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Objectives
-+
-+Service Discovery SHALL provide:
-+
-+- Deterministic service selection
-+- Capability-based discovery
-+- Version compatibility
-+- Contract verification
-+- Dependency awareness
-+- Governance compliance
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Lifecycle
-+
-+A discovery operation SHALL progress through:
-+
-+1. Receive Discovery Request
-+2. Validate Request
-+3. Query Service Registry
-+4. Filter Candidate Services
-+5. Verify Compatibility
-+6. Select Service
-+7. Record Discovery Result
-+
-+Every stage SHALL be auditable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Request
-+
-+Every discovery request SHALL specify:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Request ID | Yes | Unique discovery request identifier |
-+| Workflow ID | Yes | Associated workflow |
-+| Workflow Version | Yes | Workflow version |
-+| Required Capability | Yes | Requested capability |
-+| Required Contract | Yes | Required service contract |
-+| Required Schema Version | Yes | Required schema version |
-+| Correlation ID | Yes | Workflow correlation identifier |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental request information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Candidate Selection
-+
-+Candidate services SHALL be filtered according to:
-+
-+- Registry status
-+- Supported capability
-+- Supported contract
-+- Workflow compatibility
-+- Schema compatibility
-+- Version compatibility
-+
-+Only Approved and Active services SHALL be considered.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Compatibility Verification
-+
-+Service compatibility SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Service Contract
-+- Workflow Version
-+- Schema Version
-+- Event Version
-+- Repository Version
-+- API Version
-+
-+Incompatible services SHALL be rejected.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Deterministic Selection
-+
-+When multiple compatible services exist, selection SHALL follow deterministic rules.
-+
-+Selection priority SHOULD consider:
-+
-+1. Explicit workflow configuration
-+2. Governance policy
-+3. Highest compatible version
-+4. Stable ordering by Service ID
-+
-+Selection SHALL NOT depend upon runtime randomness.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dependency Resolution
-+
-+Discovery SHALL verify service dependencies before selection.
-+
-+Dependencies MAY include:
-+
-+- Supporting services
-+- Repository components
-+- Event infrastructure
-+- External systems
-+
-+Unsatisfied dependencies SHALL prevent service selection.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Response
-+
-+Every successful discovery SHALL return:
-+
-+- Service ID
-+- Service Name
-+- Service Version
-+- Contract Version
-+- Capability
-+- Compatibility Status
-+- Registry Reference
-+- Discovery Timestamp
-+
-+Responses SHALL preserve provenance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Failure
-+
-+Discovery MAY fail because of:
-+
-+- Missing capability
-+- Contract incompatibility
-+- Schema incompatibility
-+- Dependency failure
-+- Governance restrictions
-+- Registry inconsistency
-+
-+Failures SHALL generate structured diagnostic information.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Caching
-+
-+Implementations MAY cache discovery results.
-+
-+Cached results SHALL:
-+
-+- Reference registry versions.
-+- Respect governance policies.
-+- Expire according to repository configuration.
-+- Be invalidated following registry updates.
-+
-+Caching SHALL NOT compromise deterministic selection.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Discovery Events
-+
-+Discovery operations SHALL publish events including:
-+
-+- Discovery Requested
-+- Discovery Started
-+- Candidates Identified
-+- Compatibility Verified
-+- Service Selected
-+- Discovery Failed
-+
-+Events SHALL conform to the Event Model Specification.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Requirements
-+
-+Every discovery operation SHALL record:
-+
-+- Discovery Request ID
-+- Workflow ID
-+- Correlation ID
-+- Selected Service
-+- Selection Criteria
-+- Compatibility Results
-+- Timestamp
-+- Outcome
-+
-+Audit records SHALL remain immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Discovery services SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Discovery requests
-+- Successful discoveries
-+- Failed discoveries
-+- Registry query duration
-+- Compatibility failures
-+- Cache utilization
-+- Service selection frequency
-+
-+Monitoring SHALL support operational optimization.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Discovery SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Request schema
-+- Workflow compatibility
-+- Registry consistency
-+- Contract compatibility
-+- Dependency integrity
-+- Governance approval
-+
-+Validation SHALL complete before service selection.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Service Discovery integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Service Registry
-+- Workflow Service Contracts
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Workflow Governance
-+- Repository Indexes
-+- Event Processing
-+- Observability
-+
-+Discovery SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Workflow orchestration depends upon locating the correct service, not merely any available service.
-+
-+By treating service discovery as a governed, deterministic capability grounded in the authoritative Service Registry, the Repository Ingestion Framework ensures that workflow execution remains reproducible, interoperable, and resilient as services evolve over time.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
