-+# Workflow Service Dispatch Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Service Dispatch Specification defines the canonical architecture for dispatching validated workflow execution requests to eligible service instances within the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Dispatch is responsible for transforming routing decisions into executable work assignments while preserving execution integrity, service contracts, provenance, repository consistency, and operational governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Dispatch follows routing.
-+- Dispatch is deterministic.
-+- Dispatch preserves execution context.
-+- Dispatch is policy-driven.
-+- Dispatch decisions are observable.
-+- Dispatch is fully auditable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Services
-+- Parser Services
-+- Validation Services
-+- Mapping Services
-+- Repository Services
-+- Publication Services
-+- Event Services
-+- Governance Services
-+- Utility Services
-+- Administrative Services
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Definition
-+
-+Workflow Service Dispatch is the governed process of assigning an approved execution request to a specific service instance after routing, validation, and eligibility verification have completed.
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL assign work without modifying workflow semantics.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Objectives
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL provide:
-+
-+- Deterministic work assignment
-+- Context preservation
-+- Execution readiness
-+- Resource-aware assignment
-+- Failure-aware assignment
-+- Operational traceability
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Dispatch Schema
-+
-+Every dispatch operation SHALL contain:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Dispatch ID | Yes | Unique dispatch identifier |
-+| Workflow ID | Yes | Associated workflow |
-+| Execution ID | Yes | Execution identifier |
-+| Dispatch Timestamp | Yes | Assignment timestamp |
-+| Source Component | Yes | Originating coordinator |
-+| Target Service | Yes | Destination service |
-+| Target Instance | Yes | Assigned service instance |
-+| Dispatch Policy | Yes | Governing dispatch policy |
-+| Assignment Status | Yes | Dispatch outcome |
-+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental dispatch information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Prerequisites
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL occur only after:
-+
-+- Workflow validation
-+- Routing completion
-+- Service discovery
-+- Capability verification
-+- Contract verification
-+- Dependency validation
-+- Health verification
-+- Authorization
-+
-+Incomplete prerequisites SHALL prevent dispatch.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Target Selection
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL assign work only to instances that satisfy:
-+
-+- Active lifecycle state
-+- Healthy operational status
-+- Compatible capabilities
-+- Compatible contracts
-+- Available execution capacity
-+- Repository accessibility
-+
-+Selection SHALL remain deterministic.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Assignment Policies
-+
-+Supported assignment policies include:
-+
-+- Single Instance Assignment
-+- Affinity Assignment
-+- Priority Assignment
-+- Capacity-Based Assignment
-+- Health-Aware Assignment
-+- Recovery Assignment
-+- Administrative Assignment
-+
-+Assignment policies SHALL be explicitly declared.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Execution Context
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL preserve the complete execution context including:
-+
-+- Workflow ID
-+- Execution ID
-+- Correlation ID
-+- Repository Context
-+- Security Context
-+- Configuration Context
-+- Provenance ID
-+- Checkpoint References
-+
-+Context SHALL remain unchanged throughout dispatch.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Resource Verification
-+
-+Prior to assignment, dispatch SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Compute availability
-+- Memory availability
-+- Storage availability
-+- Queue capacity
-+- Network connectivity
-+- Dependency readiness
-+
-+Resource shortages SHALL invoke governed exception handling.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Lifecycle
-+
-+Dispatch operations SHALL progress through the following lifecycle:
-+
-+Requested
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Validated
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Prepared
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Assigned
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Acknowledged
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Executing
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Completed
-+
-+or
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Failed
-+
-+Lifecycle transitions SHALL be recorded.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Acknowledgement
-+
-+Assigned services SHALL acknowledge dispatch.
-+
-+Acknowledgement SHALL confirm:
-+
-+- Assignment acceptance
-+- Context integrity
-+- Resource readiness
-+- Contract compatibility
-+- Execution readiness
-+
-+Missing acknowledgements SHALL trigger timeout handling.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Timeout Handling
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL define timeout behavior for:
-+
-+- Assignment delay
-+- Acknowledgement timeout
-+- Resource acquisition
-+- Initialization
-+- Execution start
-+
-+Timeouts SHALL generate operational events.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Failure Handling
-+
-+Dispatch failures MAY result from:
-+
-+- Target unavailable
-+- Validation failure
-+- Authorization failure
-+- Resource exhaustion
-+- Dependency failure
-+- Health degradation
-+- Communication failure
-+
-+Failures SHALL invoke approved recovery or fallback policies.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Retry Policy
-+
-+Dispatch retries SHALL specify:
-+
-+- Retry conditions
-+- Maximum attempts
-+- Retry interval
-+- Alternative target selection
-+- Escalation threshold
-+
-+Retry behavior SHALL preserve workflow determinism.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Constraints
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL enforce:
-+
-+- Contract compliance
-+- Capability compatibility
-+- Version compatibility
-+- Scheduling policies
-+- Security policies
-+- Repository governance
-+
-+Constraint violations SHALL prevent assignment.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Dispatch validation SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Workflow eligibility
-+- Service eligibility
-+- Instance eligibility
-+- Execution context integrity
-+- Repository connectivity
-+- Policy compliance
-+
-+Invalid dispatch operations SHALL be rejected.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dispatch Events
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL publish events including:
-+
-+- Dispatch Requested
-+- Dispatch Validated
-+- Dispatch Prepared
-+- Dispatch Assigned
-+- Dispatch Acknowledged
-+- Dispatch Started
-+- Dispatch Completed
-+- Dispatch Failed
-+- Dispatch Retried
-+- Dispatch Cancelled
-+
-+Events SHALL conform to the Event Model Specification.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Requirements
-+
-+Dispatch activities SHALL record:
-+
-+- Dispatch ID
-+- Workflow ID
-+- Execution ID
-+- Target service
-+- Target instance
-+- Assignment policy
-+- Validation outcome
-+- Timestamp
-+- Provenance reference
-+
-+Audit records SHALL remain immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Dispatch services SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Dispatch requests
-+- Successful assignments
-+- Failed assignments
-+- Assignment latency
-+- Acknowledgement latency
-+- Retry frequency
-+- Dispatch throughput
-+- Policy violations
-+
-+Monitoring SHALL support operational governance and execution optimization.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Security
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL:
-+
-+- Authenticate requesting components.
-+- Authorize assignment operations.
-+- Protect execution context.
-+- Validate service identity.
-+- Record privileged administrative actions.
-+
-+Unauthorized dispatch SHALL be prohibited.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Service Dispatch integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Service Routing
-+- Workflow Service Discovery
-+- Workflow Service Registry
-+- Workflow Service Health
-+- Workflow Service Load Balancing
-+- Workflow Service Scheduling
-+- Workflow Service Coordination
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Event Processing
-+- Observability
-+- Repository Indexes
-+
-+Dispatch SHALL preserve repository integrity, deterministic execution, and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Dispatch is the operational bridge between architectural planning and executable work.
-+
-+By representing dispatch as a governed, deterministic, and auditable repository capability, the Repository Ingestion Framework ensures that every execution assignment is reproducible, policy-compliant, context-preserving, and fully traceable throughout the lifecycle of every workflow execution.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
