-+# Workflow Service Health Specification
-+
-+**Version:** 0.1  
-+**Status:** Draft  
-+**Subsystem:** Repository Ingestion Framework
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Purpose
-+
-+The Workflow Service Health Specification defines the canonical framework for evaluating, reporting, and governing the operational health of services participating in the Repository Ingestion Framework.
-+
-+Service Health provides authoritative operational visibility that supports workflow execution, service discovery, dependency management, orchestration, and operational governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Principles
-+
-+- Health evaluation is deterministic.
-+- Health information is observable.
-+- Health assessments are evidence-based.
-+- Health reporting preserves provenance.
-+- Health evaluations are independently verifiable.
-+- Health information is implementation-independent.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Scope
-+
-+This specification applies to:
-+
-+- Workflow Services
-+- Parser Services
-+- Validation Services
-+- Mapping Services
-+- Repository Services
-+- Event Services
-+- Governance Services
-+- Utility Services
-+- Administrative Services
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Definition
-+
-+Service Health is the measured operational condition of a service at a specific point in time.
-+
-+Health SHALL be derived from observable operational evidence rather than subjective assessment.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Objectives
-+
-+Service Health SHALL provide:
-+
-+- Operational readiness
-+- Service availability
-+- Dependency awareness
-+- Failure detection
-+- Capacity assessment
-+- Governance visibility
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Health Schema
-+
-+Every health assessment SHALL contain:
-+
-+| Field | Required | Description |
-+|--------|----------|-------------|
-+| Health Record ID | Yes | Unique health record identifier |
-+| Service ID | Yes | Evaluated service |
-+| Assessment Timestamp | Yes | Time of assessment |
-+| Health Status | Yes | Current operational condition |
-+| Availability | Yes | Availability measurement |
-+| Dependency Status | Yes | Dependency evaluation |
-+| Performance Status | Yes | Performance assessment |
-+| Validation Status | Yes | Validation outcome |
-+| Assessment Source | Yes | Responsible monitoring component |
-+| Provenance ID | Yes | Provenance reference |
-+| Metadata | No | Supplemental health information |
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Status
-+
-+Every service SHALL exist in one of the following health states:
-+
-+- Unknown
-+- Initializing
-+- Healthy
-+- Degraded
-+- Unhealthy
-+- Recovering
-+- Maintenance
-+- Offline
-+
-+Health status SHALL remain mutually exclusive.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Healthy
-+
-+Healthy indicates:
-+
-+- Service is available.
-+- Required dependencies are healthy.
-+- Performance is within acceptable thresholds.
-+- Validation succeeds.
-+- Service is eligible for workflow execution.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Degraded
-+
-+Degraded indicates:
-+
-+- Core functionality remains available.
-+- Performance or capacity has declined.
-+- Optional capabilities MAY be unavailable.
-+- Execution MAY continue under governance policy.
-+
-+Degraded services SHALL remain observable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Unhealthy
-+
-+Unhealthy indicates:
-+
-+- Critical failures exist.
-+- Required capabilities are unavailable.
-+- Workflow execution SHOULD be prevented.
-+- Recovery SHOULD be initiated.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Recovering
-+
-+Recovering indicates:
-+
-+- Recovery procedures are active.
-+- Service validation is in progress.
-+- Operational readiness has not yet been confirmed.
-+
-+Recovering services SHALL be reassessed before becoming Healthy.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Maintenance
-+
-+Maintenance indicates:
-+
-+- Service is intentionally unavailable.
-+- Administrative maintenance is underway.
-+- Workflow execution SHALL follow governance policy.
-+
-+Maintenance periods SHALL be scheduled where practical.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Offline
-+
-+Offline indicates:
-+
-+- Service is unavailable.
-+- Discovery SHALL exclude the service.
-+- Dependencies SHALL be evaluated accordingly.
-+
-+Offline status SHALL generate operational events.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Indicators
-+
-+Health assessments SHOULD evaluate:
-+
-+- Availability
-+- Response time
-+- Error rate
-+- Resource utilization
-+- Queue utilization
-+- Dependency health
-+- Validation success
-+- Event publication
-+- Repository connectivity
-+
-+Indicators SHALL use measurable criteria.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Assessment
-+
-+Health assessment SHALL include:
-+
-+1. Service availability
-+2. Dependency verification
-+3. Contract validation
-+4. Capability verification
-+5. Performance evaluation
-+6. Repository connectivity
-+7. Event publication verification
-+8. Final health determination
-+
-+Assessment SHALL remain deterministic.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Dependency Assessment
-+
-+Dependency evaluation SHALL verify:
-+
-+- Provider availability
-+- Version compatibility
-+- Contract compatibility
-+- Response behavior
-+- Repository accessibility
-+
-+Dependency failures SHALL influence overall health status.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Thresholds
-+
-+Thresholds MAY be defined for:
-+
-+- Response latency
-+- Error percentage
-+- Queue depth
-+- Memory utilization
-+- CPU utilization
-+- Storage utilization
-+- Dependency failures
-+
-+Threshold definitions SHALL be governed through Configuration Management.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health Events
-+
-+Health monitoring SHALL publish events including:
-+
-+- Health Assessment Started
-+- Service Healthy
-+- Service Degraded
-+- Service Unhealthy
-+- Service Recovering
-+- Service Offline
-+- Maintenance Started
-+- Maintenance Completed
-+
-+Events SHALL conform to the Event Model Specification.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Health History
-+
-+Historical health assessments SHALL:
-+
-+- Remain immutable.
-+- Preserve timestamps.
-+- Preserve provenance.
-+- Support trend analysis.
-+- Support incident investigation.
-+
-+Historical records SHALL NOT be modified.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Validation
-+
-+Health assessments SHALL validate:
-+
-+- Service identity
-+- Monitoring integrity
-+- Assessment completeness
-+- Dependency consistency
-+- Repository connectivity
-+- Schema compliance
-+
-+Invalid assessments SHALL be rejected.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Monitoring
-+
-+Health monitoring SHOULD expose:
-+
-+- Healthy services
-+- Degraded services
-+- Unhealthy services
-+- Offline services
-+- Health transition frequency
-+- Assessment latency
-+- Monitoring failures
-+
-+Monitoring SHALL support operational governance.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Audit Requirements
-+
-+Health management SHALL record:
-+
-+- Service ID
-+- Assessment timestamp
-+- Health status
-+- Assessment criteria
-+- Monitoring component
-+- Validation results
-+- Provenance reference
-+
-+Audit records SHALL remain immutable.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Repository Integration
-+
-+Workflow Service Health integrates with:
-+
-+- Workflow Service Registry
-+- Workflow Service Discovery
-+- Workflow Service Dependencies
-+- Workflow Orchestration
-+- Workflow Execution
-+- Configuration Management
-+- Observability
-+- Event Processing
-+- Repository Indexes
-+
-+Health management SHALL preserve repository integrity and institutional accountability.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Design Philosophy
-+
-+Reliable workflow execution depends upon reliable services.
-+
-+By treating service health as a governed repository asset rather than a transient operational signal, the Repository Ingestion Framework provides a trustworthy foundation for orchestration, discovery, recovery, governance, and continuous operational improvement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+End of Specification.
-\ No newline at end of file
