-+# ADE_ACTIVE_STATE_BOOTSTRAP_v2
-+Version: 2.0
-+Status: Active
-+Purpose: Bootstrap the next engineering session while preserving methodology, architectural state, and project philosophy.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Project Identity
-+
-+ADE is a longitudinal knowledge stewardship and repository engineering project.
-+
-+The repository is not the origin of the project.
-+
-+The repository is the canonical representation of an extensive design corpus developed across many ChatGPT conversations.
-+
-+Those conversations constitute primary design provenance.
-+
-+Canonical Markdown is the authoritative implementation.
-+
-+The repository exists to preserve not only *what* was decided, but *why* it was decided.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Guiding Principles
-+
-+1. Preserve the reasoning, not just the result.
-+
-+2. Search before designing.
-+
-+3. Assume mature implementations may already exist within the corpus.
-+
-+4. Prefer refinement over reinvention.
-+
-+5. Canonical documents represent current truth.
-+
-+6. Conversation history represents architectural provenance.
-+
-+7. Repository evolution should be evidence-driven.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Current Methodology
-+
-+For every significant feature:
-+
-+Search corpus
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Recover prior work
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Evaluate
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Compare with current implementation
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Refine if necessary
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Promote to canonical Markdown
-+
-+↓
-+
-+Automate repetitive processes where practical
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Immediate Objective
-+
-+Repository Archaeology
-+
-+Treat the uploaded conversation corpus as the primary engineering record.
-+
-+Recover mature concepts before creating new architecture.
-+
-+Examples include:
-+
-+• OBS framework
-+• Governance
-+• Repository Constitution
-+• Specifications
-+• Automation
-+• Knowledge refinement
-+• Metadata
-+• Health metrics
-+• Workflow
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Current Understanding
-+
-+Recent conversations have produced substantial architectural improvements.
-+
-+These improvements are assumed compatible with historical work unless evidence indicates otherwise.
-+
-+The objective is integration—not replacement.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Canonical Rule
-+
-+Current repository documents remain authoritative until corpus evidence demonstrates a superior implementation.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Conversation Processing Standard
-+
-+Every engineering conversation is itself an engineering artifact.
-+
-+Each completed chat should generate a structured summary suitable for repository inclusion.
-+
-+Suggested artifact:
-+
-+CHAT_SUMMARY_<YYYYMMDD>_<topic>.md
-+
-+Recommended sections:
-+
-+---
-+
-+Metadata
-+
-+• Date
-+• Session number
-+• Duration (optional)
-+• Primary objectives
-+• Repository version
-+
-+---
-+
-+Major Decisions
-+
-+Chronological record of significant engineering decisions.
-+
-+---
-+
-+Architectural Changes
-+
-+New structures
-+Modified structures
-+Deprecated ideas
-+
-+---
-+
-+Recovered Concepts
-+
-+Historical concepts rediscovered from corpus.
-+
-+---
-+
-+New Concepts
-+
-+Ideas originating during the session.
-+
-+---
-+
-+Integration Decisions
-+
-+How new and historical concepts were reconciled.
-+
-+---
-+
-+Action Items
-+
-+Ordered implementation tasks.
-+
-+---
-+
-+Open Questions
-+
-+Outstanding engineering questions.
-+
-+---
-+
-+Repository Impact
-+
-+Files to create
-+
-+Files to modify
-+
-+Automation opportunities
-+
-+Governance implications
-+
-+Documentation implications
-+
-+---
-+
-+Observations
-+
-+Candidate OBS-(n)
-+
-+Potential ADRs
-+
-+Lessons learned
-+
-+---
-+
-+Conversation Assessment
-+
-+What worked well.
-+
-+What should change next session.
-+
-+---
-+
-+# Future Artifact Types
-+
-+Repository Constitution
-+
-+Architecture Decision Records (ADR)
-+
-+OBS observations
-+
-+Specifications
-+
-+Governance
-+
-+Standards
-+
-+Templates
-+
-+Automation scripts
-+
-+Chat summaries
